1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was '''NOT''' the son of Shahrijar ben Bostanai or the son of Bostanai himself. '''Surkhab I of the Bavandids was the son of Farrukhzad.''' The link to Bostanai was part of a claim of descent from King David. Ma
2 CONC ny rulers claimed descent from David, but in all likeliness, the line is fake and not to be taken seriously. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surkhab_I '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Surkhab I''' (Persian: سهراب) was the second ruler of the Bavand dynasty from ca. 673 to 717.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Farrukhzad, a Parthian nobleman from the Ispahbudhan family, a family which had a long story of service to the Sasanians, tracing his descent back to Bawi. Surkhab also had four brothers named Isfandyadh, Shahram
2 CONC , Bahram, and Farrukhan. In 665, Farrukhzad was murdered by an Karenid named Valash, who then had his domains conquered. After the murder of his father, Surkhab fled to a Bavand stronghold in Mazandaran. In 673, Surkhab avenged hi
2 CONC s father by killing Valash, and then reconquered lost Bavand territory. He then crowned himself as ispahbadh of the Bavandids at his capital in Perim. Surkhab died in 717, and was succeeded by his son Mihr Mardan.
2 CONT
