2 CONT
2 CONT == Ashot III of Armenia==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Abas I, King of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * ABAS, son of SMBAT I King of Armenia & his wife --- (-951).  ... He succeeded his brother in [928] as ABAS King of Armenia.   m ---.  The name of Abas's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==King Abas & his wife had five children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         '''ASHOT (-977).'''  The Tables chronologiques of Samuel of Ani record the succession in 954 of "Achot fils d´Abas"[95].  He succeeded his father in 951 as '''ASHOT III "Voghormadz/the Merciful" King of Armenia.'''  He
2 CONC  moved his capital from Kars to Ani where he was crowned in 961.  Kirakos Ganjaketsi's History of Armenia records that many bishops "gathered in the fortress of Ani in the kingdom of Ashot, son of Abas" to discuss unity with the G
2 CONC eorgian church[96].  He resisted the advance of the Byzantine army of Emperor Ioannes Tzimisces, who recognised King Ashot's authority in 974 faced with Armenia's combined military forces[97].  m ---.  The name of Ashot's wife is 
2 CONC not known.  Ashot & his wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT **a)         SMBAT (-[989/90]).  Kirakos Ganjaketsi's History of Armenia records that "his son Smbat (called Shahnshah)" succeeded Ashot and ruled for thirteen years, starting the construction of the cathedral at Ani[98].  The His
2 CONC tory of Aristakes Lastivertci names "Gagik son of Ashot, brother of Smbat and Gurgen from the Bagratid clan" as king of Armenia[99].  He succeeded his father in 977 as SMBAT II "Tiezerakal/Master of the Universe" King of Armenia. 
2 CONC  His  succession was challenged by his uncle Mushel, although they were reconciled in [982][100].  
2 CONT
2 CONT **b)         GAGIK (-[1017/20]).  The History of Aristakes Lastivertci names "Gagik son of Ashot, brother of Smbat and Gurgen from the Bagratid clan" as king of Armenia[101].  He succeeded his brother in [989/90] as GAGIK I "the G
2 CONC reat" King of Armenia.  -        see below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT **c)         GURGEN [Kiwrike] (-989).  The History of Aristakes Lastivertci names "Gagik son of Ashot, brother of Smbat and Gurgen from the Bagratid clan" as king of Armenia[102].  His father granted him the northern district of T
2 CONC ashir in [972], where he adopted the title King of Albania[103].  -        see Part E.  
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         MUSHEL (-984).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  His brother King Ashot III installed him at Kars in 961, where he adopted the royal title in 963[104].  m ---.  The name of 
2 CONC Mushel's wife is not known.  -        KINGS of KARS and VANAND.  
2 CONT
2 CONT == Ashot III==
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashot III the Merciful (Armenian: Աշոտ Գ. Ողորմած) also known as Ashot the Gracious (952/953-977) was an Armenian king. He ruled from Armenia's capital city of Ani.
2 CONT
2 CONT Armenia reached the height of its golden era during the reign of the Kings Abas I (928-951), Ashot III (952/953-977), and his sons Smbat II (X) (977-989) and Gagik I (990-1020), an era which according to Muyldermans “in regard to 
2 CONC its brilliance and glory was unique.” Ashot III won the favour of the caliphate by defeating one of the emirs in Azerbaijan who had revolted against Baghdad and attacked Armenia. During the war between the Byzantine emperor John T
2 CONC zimiskes and the Arabs, Armenia did its best to remain neutral and forced the two battling parties to respect the boundaries of its country. The Byzantine army began to march across the plain of Moush, thinking to strike the decis
2 CONC ive blow against the Arabs from Armenia, but when they met with the 30,000 strong army of Ashot III, they altered their plan and left Armenia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Prince Taros, fl. 1000, father of Ruben, Governor of Larisse in 1025, and grandfather of Prince John-Smbat, who was the father of Ruben I of Armenia.
2 CONT
