2 CONT '''Eudokia Makrembolitissa''' (Greek: ''Εὐδοκία Μακρεμβολίτισσα'', romanized: ''Evdokía Makremvolítissa'') was a Byzantine empress by her successive marriages to Constantine X Doukas and Romanos IV Diogenes. She acted as regent of
2 CONC  her minor son, Michael VII in 1067, and resigned her regency by marriage to Romanos IV Diogenes. When he was deposed in 1071 she resumed the regency for her sons, but was soon forced to resign again.
2 CONT
2 CONT Because she essentially ruled in her own right during her sole regencies and retained the title of empress, several modern scholars consider Eudokia to have been empress regnant in 1067 and some also in 1071.
2 CONT
2 CONT #  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eudokia_Makrembolitissa#Background_and_early_life  '''Background and early life''']
2 CONT #  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eudokia_Makrembolitissa#Empress   '''Empress''']
2 CONT #  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eudokia_Makrembolitissa#Later_life '''Later life''']
2 CONT #  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eudokia_Makrembolitissa#Issue  ''' Issue:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/93LJ-J5W/empress-eudoxia-makrembolitissa-1030-1096
2 CONT
2 CONT  By her first husband, Eudokia had seven children, four sons and three daughters: 
2 CONT *Michael VII Doukas, co-emperor from 1060 and senior emperor after 1071.
2 CONT *A son who died in infancy.
2 CONT *Anne Doukaina, nun.
2 CONT *Andronikos Doukas, co-emperor from 1068 to 1078.
2 CONT *Theodora Doukaina, who married Domenico Selvo, Doge of Venice.
2 CONT *Konstantios Doukas, co-emperor from 1060 to 1078, died in battle with the Normans in 1081.
2 CONT *Zoe Doukaina, who married Adrianos Komnenos, a brother of Emperor Alexios I Komnenos. 
2 CONT **They had a son, Alexios, and two daughters, maybe named Anne and Alexia.
2 CONT
2 CONT   By her second husband, she had two sons, most likely twins: 
2 CONT *Nikephoros Diogenes, blinded by order of Alexios I Comnenus on charges of treason.
2 CONT *Leo Diogenes, died in battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapter 20.  MAKREMBOLITES
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTINE%20NOBILITY.htm#EvdokiaMakrembolitissadied1096
