2 CONT Two brothers, parents not known: 
2 CONT *1.         THEODOSIOS Monomachos ... Theodosios Monomachos & his wife had three known children: a)         KONSTANTINOS Monomachos ([1005/1010]-11 Jan 1055, bur Monastery of Mangana). b)         POULCHERIA (-after [1043/44]).  Ps
2 CONC ellos names the emperor's "own sister Pulcheria…one of the cleverest women of our generation" when recording that she advised her brother not to recall his mistress from exile[1681].  In another passage, Psellos states that "Const
2 CONC antine had two sisters, the elder…Helena, the younger Euprepia"[1682].  It is not known whether one of these may have been the same person as Pulcheria.  c)         HELENA (-[1050]). d)         EUPREPIA (-after 1055).  
2 CONT * 2.         ['''--- Monomachos''' .  His parentage is confirmed by Cedrenus who records that "Theodosius præses, patruo Monomachi natus" opposed the succession of "Michaelum Stratioticum" as emperor (in 1056)[1689], on the assump
2 CONC tion that "patruus" should be interpreted in its strict sense of paternal uncle, although this is not beyond all doubt.  It is should be noted that neither of the sources cited below refer to his son as "Monomachos".]  m ---.  One
2 CONC  child:  a)         THEODOSIOS [Monomachos] (-after 1056).  m ---.  The name of Theodosios's wife is not known.  Theodosios & his wife had one child:  i)          --- [Monomachos] (-after 1056).  Cedrenus records that "Theodosius 
2 CONC præses, patruo Monomachi natus" sought refuge "cum filio" in Hagia Sofia (in 1056)[1693]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
