2 CONT =Chapter 31.  SYNADENOS=
2 CONT
2 CONT *4.         THEODOULOS Synadenos.  A seal dated to [1065] names "Theodoulos Synadenos, vestarches"[519].  m --- Botaneiatissa, sister of Emperor NIKEFOROS III, daughter of --- Botaneiates & his wife ---. 
2 CONT **  a)         --- Synadene. m ([1066/75]) as his second wife, GÉZA of Hungary, son of BÉLA I King of Hungary & his wife Ryksa of Poland ([1044/45]-25 Apr 1077)
2 CONT **  b)         '''[NIKEFOROS Synadenos (-killed in battle Durazzo 18 Oct 1081).'''  The Alexeiad names "a certain Synadenos of Levantine origin…a family relative of Nikeforos" when recording that Emperor Nikeforos Botaneiates plan
2 CONC ned to name him as his successor, but does not specify the precise relationship[527].  If, as indicated above, the wife of Theodoulos Synadenos was the sister of Emperor Nikeforos, it is likely that he was the father of Nikeforos 
2 CONC Synadenos, although this is not without all doubt.  The Alexeiad records the death of "Nikeforos surnamed Synadenos" fighting Robert "Guiscard" Duke of Apulia in Durazzo in 1081[528].  Betrothed to ZOE porphyrogeneta Doukaina, dau
2 CONC ghter of Emperor KONSTANTINOS X & his second wife Evdokia Makrembolitissa (1062-before 1136).] 
