1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anushirvan_Sharaf_al-Ma%27ali '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anushirvan Sharaf al-Ma'ali''' was the ruler of the Ziyarids (c. 1030-1050). He was the son of Manuchihr.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his father's death, Anushirvan became the Ziyarid ruler. His ascension was confirmed by Mahmud of Ghazna, in exchange for a promise that tribute would continue to be paid by the Ziyarids. In 1032, however, Anushirvan's army c
2 CONC hief and maternal relative Abu Kalijar ibn Vayhan effectively took control of the state. Mahmud's successor Mas'ud recognized this change upon being assured that the tribute would still be paid, and in 1033 married one of Abu Kali
2 CONC jar's daughters. The Ziyarid tribute was not regularly paid, however, leading to a Ghaznavid invasion in 1035. Mas'ud's army marched as far as Royan, forcing Abu Kalijar to flee. When the Ghaznavids left, however, Abu Kalijar rega
2 CONC ined control of the state and made peace with Mas'ud, promising to pay the tribute.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after 1040, Anushirvan managed to arrest Abu Kalijar and resumed the rule on his own. In 1041 or 1042, however, the Seljuks under Toghril Beg conquered Gurgan. Toghril Beg installed a former Ghaznavid commander, Mardavij 
2 CONC ibn Bishui as governor of the region. Mardavij eventually made peace with Anushirvan, causing the latter to accept Toghril as his overlord. The Ziyarids would remain as Seljuk vassals until the last quarter of the 11th century. An
2 CONC ushirvan died in 1050, and was succeeded by cousin Keikavus.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT * E. Merçil (1989). Gazneliler Devleti Tarihi (History of Ghaznavids), Türk Tarih Kurumu, Ankara. ISBN 975-16-0189-4
2 CONT * R. N. Frye (1975). The Cambridge History of Iran, Volume Four: From the Arab Invasion to the Saljuqs. ISBN 0-521-20093-8
