1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shahrbaraz belonged to the House of Mihran,[1] one of the Seven Parthian clans; he was the son of a certain Ardashir. During Shahrbaraz's later life, he joined the Sasanian army, where he rose to high offices, and 
2 CONC was appointed as spahbed of Nēmrōz. He was married to the sister of the Sasanian king Khosrau II, Mirhran, whom Shahrbaraz had one boy with named Shapur-i Shahrvaraz.
