2 CONT 1.         ANDRONIKOS Kontostefanos (-1156 or after).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' THEODORA Komnene, daughter of ADRIANOS Komnenos & his wife --- ([1110]-).  Gautier records her parentage and marriage[421].  Andronikos Kontostefanos & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         IOANNES Kontostefanos (-after 1166).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Sébastos.  The record of the synod of 6 Mar 1166 records the presence of “...consobrinis...nostri regi
2 CONC s Contostephanis domino Joanne et domino Alexio... pansebasto sebasto domino Joanne Contostephano...”[422]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         ALEXIOS Kontostefanos.  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  The record of the synod in Sep 1191 records “...Alexis Contostéphane pansébaste sebaste et chartulaire...”, whom Sti
2 CONC ernon identifies as Alexios, son of Stefanos Kontostefanos (see above)[423].  However, if the death of the latter is correctly dated to 1176 (as shown above, but no primary source has yet been identified which confirms this date),
2 CONC  it is more likely that Alexios who is named in Sep 1191 was the son of Andronikos Kontostefanos and his wife Theodora Komnene.  m [MARIA Doukaina, daughter of ---].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been
2 CONC  identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *c)         --- Kontostefanina .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified
