1 NOTE Romanus I Lecapenus, from Armenia, married the widow of Leo VI, Zoe II.  Romanus seized control of the Eastern Roman Empire during the minority of his stepson, Constantine VII from 919-944.  Romanus had been a common soldier, and 
2 CONC after marrying the widown, crowned himself emperor, not schooled, and said to be "ignorant"  he nevertheless was an able administrator, and tried to establish a new dynasty, but was deposed by Constantine in 944.  His dynasty did 
2 CONC live on, as his daughter, Helena married Constantine, and was the mother of Romanus II.  Romanus died in 948.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sons of Romanus I Lecapenus was made him prisoner;  his sons, Christophorus, Stephanus, Constantine, and Theophylactus;  whose interests the father had tried to serve by building an empire. Romanus I later died in 948, and his
2 CONC  kingdom taken over by his step-son/ son-in-law Constantine VII.
