2 CONT '''Stephen Lekapenos''' or '''Lecapenus''' (Ancient Greek: Στέφανος Λακαπηνός or Λεκαπηνός, romanized: Stéphanos Lakapēnos or Lekapēnos; died 18 April 963) was the second son of the Byzantine emperor Romanos I Lekapenos (r. 920–94
2 CONC 4), and co-emperor from 924 to 945. With his younger brother Constantine, he deposed Romanos I in December 944, but they were overthrown and exiled a few weeks later by their brother in law, the legitimate emperor Constantine VII 
2 CONC (r. 913–959). Stephen lived out his life in exile on the island of Lesbos, where he died on Easter 963. .. ...
