2 CONT 5.         THEODORA Komnene ([1053]-after [1094/95]).  Nikeforos Bryennios names (in order) "Maria, Eudocia et Theodora" as the three daughters of "Ioanni" and his wife Anna[120].  Nikeforos Bryennios records the marriage, after h
2 CONC er father's death "matris voluntate", of "Ioannes…Comnenus curopalates…postrema Theodora [filia]" and "Constantino Diogenis iam imperatoris filio"[121].  The Alexeiad names "Theodora, the emperor's sister…widow of Diogenes's murde
2 CONC red son" when recording her reaction to an imposter pretending to be her husband who had been killed in Antioch[122].  The text names the son "Leon" but it is clear from the context that it must refer to Konstantinos, who was kill
2 CONC ed when his half-brother Leon was still an infant.  She became a nun as XENA.  m ([1068/71]) KONSTANTINOS Diogenes, son of Emperor ROMANOS Diogenes & his first wife [Anna] Alusiane [of Bulgaria] (-killed in battle Antioch [1074]).
2 CONC
2 CONT
