1 NOTE Constantine VIII Emperor of the Eastern Roman Empire died age 68 in 1028.  His daughter, Zoe, then age 48 succeeded him, and married  60 year old Romanus III Argyrolpolus (aka Argyrus) and makes him emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Constantine VIII was just a baby when his father, Romanus II died in 960.  Later Constantine was co-ruler of the Eastern Roman Empire (Byzantine) with his brother Basil II, until 1025 when Basil died, then as sole ruler until 1028
2 CONC .   He was succeeded by Romanus III Argyrus, who had married Constantine's daughter, Zoe.
