2 TITL From “Theodora, the last Macedonian”
1 NOTE Theodora II Empress of the Eastern Roman Empire died in 1056.  She had ruled alone after her brother-in-law Constantine IX died in 1055. Theodora was the last of the Macedonian Dynasty that ruled the Eastern Roman Empire since Jus
2 CONC tinian the Great took power in 527.  Theodora was succeeded by Michael VI Stratioticus, who was overthrown early the next year by a revolt of the barons of Anatolia.  He was succeeded by the Comnenus in 1057.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodora II of the Eastern Roman Empire, older daughter of Constantine VIII, ruled as co-empress of the empire with her younger sister Zoe between 1041 and 1050.  When Zoe died in 1050, then Theodora was left to rule.  She shared 
2 CONC the throne with Zoe's 3rd husband,  Constantine IX.
