2 CONT >>>>>>b)         [daughter .  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[66], Stenkil married the unnamed daughter of King Emund.  The primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  It is possible that the marriage 
2 CONC is uncorroborated in contemporary documentation but was assumed by later genealogists to explain Stenkil's succession as king.  However, the accession could have been justified solely on the basis of his being the king's stepson, 
2 CONC although it is not impossible that it was also confirmed by subsequent marriage to his predecessor's daughter, if indeed he had one[67].  m STENKIL Ragnvaldson, son of RAGNVALD Jarl of Västergötland & his wife Ingeborg of Norway (
2 CONC -1066).  He succeeded his father-in-law in 1060 as STENKIL King of Sweden.]
