2 CONT
2 CONT Nizhin: A district center in the Chernihiv Oblast, located on the Osetr River. The city was first mentioned in the Chronicles in 1147 under the name Unezh. The title "Unezha" comes from the phrase "Nezhatina Niva", (Ben notes: U N
2 CONC ezha, or "By Nezha") where in 1078 was fought a battle between the Russian princes and the Polovtsian hordes, during which fell Grand Prince Izyaslav Yaroslavich. In the 13th century, the city was ravaged by Tatar hordes.
2 CONT
2 CONT (No sources)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes: Another source says that it was near the town of Gorodets on the Left Bank of the Dnieper River, as it was from this port that the body of Izyaslav was transported back to Kiev.
2 CONT
