2 CONT
2 CONT Anne of Kiev was born circa 1024. She was the daughter of Jarislaus I, Grand Duke of Kiev and Ingegarde of Sweden.[1],[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Raoul Crepi.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henri I, Roi de France, son of Robert II, Roi de France and Constance d'Arles, on 29 January 1044.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa 1075.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne of Kiev and Henri I, Roi de France
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Philippe I, Roi de France+1 b. c 1052, d. 29 Jul 1108
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Hugh de Crépi, Comte de Vermandois et de Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT +3 b. 1057, d. 18 Oct 1102
2 CONT
