2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_of_Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT She had two brothers named Vsevolod and Svyatopolk. She was the second oldest of the three children. <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> Anne of Kiev (or Anna Yaroslavna) (between 1024 and 1032 – 1075), daughter of Yaroslav I of
2 CONC  Kiev and his wife Princess Ingegerd of Sweden, was the queen consort of France as the wife of Henry I, and regent for her son Philip I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his first wife, Matilda, King Henry searched the courts of Europe for a suitable bride, but could not locate a princess who was not related to him within illegal degrees of kinship. At last he sent an embassy to
2 CONC  distant Kiev, which returned with Anne (also called Agnes or Anna). Anne and Henry were married at the cathedral of Reims on 19 May 1051. As a curious fact, several daughters of Yaroslav married Catholic monarchs; Anne's older si
2 CONC ster Anastasia of Kiev, was married around 1039 to the king Andrew I of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regency
2 CONT
2 CONT For six years after Henry's death in 1060, she served as regent for Philip, who was only eight at the time. She was the first queen of France to serve as regent. Her co-regent was Count Baldwin V o
2 CONT
