1 NOTE Les Sources du Regne de Hughes Capet Revue Historique
2 CONT Tome XXVIII Paris 1891, P. Violet
2 CONT Aka: Anne of Kiev
1 NOTE Anne eller Anna av Kiev (født 1024, død 1075) var datter av Jaroslav I av Kiev og den svenske prinsessen Ingegjerd Olofsdatter, dronninggemal til Henrik I av Frankrike og regent for sin sønn Filip I av Frankrike.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE "OF KIEV"
1 NOTE OR "AGNES"; "ANNE JAROSLAVNA OF KIEVE"
1 NOTE !    (1) Queen of France
2 CONT     (2) Grand Duchess of Kiev
2 CONT     (3) Also AFN 8HJ7D0
1 NOTE !    (1) Queen of France
2 CONT     (2) Grand Duchess of Kiev
2 CONT     (3) Also AFN 8HJ7D0
1 NOTE Anne of Kiev
2 CONT Born in 1024
2 CONT Died after 1075
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne married on January 20, 1044 to Henry I Capet, King of France andthey had the following sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip I the Fair Capet, King of France, born in 1052
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Agnesa Yaroslavna Rurikide, Grand Duchess of Kiev and Queen ofFrance "Anne de Kiev" was born 1024 in Kiev, Ukraine and married 1051.She died circa 1076 in France and was buried in Villiers Abbey, LaFerte-Alais, Essonne, Franc
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Anne of Kiev was the wife of Henry I of France and thedaughter of Jaroslav I. She married Henry at the cathedral of Reims, May19, 1051 and had three sons: Philippe I, King of France, Hugues("Magnus"), and Robert. For si
2 CONC x years after his death in 1060, she servedas regent for their son, Philip, who was 7 at the time of his father'sdeath. She was the first queen of France to serve as regent. A year afterthe King's death, Anne, acting as Regent, to
2 CONC ok a passionate fancy forRaoul II (III?) de Péronne, Count of Crépy, of Valois and of the Vexin, aman whose political ambition encouraged him to repudiate his wife tomarry Anne in 1062. Accused of adultery, Raoul's wife appealed t
2 CONC o PopeAlexander II, who excommunicated Raoul and Anne. The young king Philippeforgave his mother, which was just as well, since he was to find himselfin a very similar predicament in the 1090s. Raoul died in September 1071.This in
