2 CONT 4.         LANDOLF ([1040 or after]-after Mar 1092).  Amatus names (in order) "Gisulf, Landulf, Guido…John Seurre…and Guaimar" as the five sons of Prince Guaimar when he died[1023].  A charter dated 1100 quotes three earlier chart
2 CONC ers dated Aug 1058, dividing the territories of Guaimar IV Prince of Salerno between "Domini Gisulfi…et Landulfi et Guidonis et Johannis et Guaimarii fratrum ipsius domini Gisulfi", specifying that Landolf was less than 18 years o
2 CONC ld[1024].  Amatus records that Landulf surrendered San Severino and Policastro when his brother Prince Gisulf was deposed[1025].  Gemma donated a mill at Vietri to Cava, with the consent of "domni nostri Gisulfi et Landolfi et Gui
2 CONC donis et Iohannis et Gaimarii filiorum suorum", by charter dated Dec 1070[1026].  Landolf donated property to Cava for the soul of "Imilie…coniugis mee filie quondam domni Adenolfi ducis Gagete civitatis" by charter dated Mar 1092
2 CONC [1027].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' EMILIA di Gaeta, daughter of ATENOLF I Duke of Gaeta & his wife Maria di Capua.  Landolf donated property to Cava for the soul of "Imilie…coniugis mee filie quondam domni Adenolfi ducis Gagete civitatis" by charter dated M
2 CONC ar 1092[1028].  
2 CONT
