2 CONT GUAIMAR (-after 1076).  Amatus names (in order) "Gisulf, Landulf, Guido…John Seurre…and Guaimar" as the five sons of Prince Guaimar when he died, calling the last named "the tormenter and devourer who was insatiable"[1044].  A cha
2 CONC rter dated 1100 quotes three earlier charters dated Aug 1058, dividing the territories of Guaimar IV Prince of Salerno between "Domini Gisulfi…et Landulfi et Guidonis et Johannis et Guaimarii fratrum ipsius domini Gisulfi"[1045]. 
2 CONC  Gemma donated a mill at Vietri to Cava, with the consent of "domni nostri Gisulfi et Landolfi et Guidonis et Iohannis et Gaimarii filiorum suorum", by charter dated Dec 1070[1046].  Amatus records that Guaimar surrendered Cilento
2 CONC  when his brother Prince Gisulf was deposed[1047]. 
