1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fressenda ''(c.1000-c.1060)''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fressenda''' ''(Latin: Frensendis or Fredesendis)'' was an 11th-century Norman noblewoman and the wife of Tancred of Hauteville. She is known as the mother of Robert Guiscard and Roger I of Sicily.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Fressenda, wife of Tancred de Hauteville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents unknown. NB: the historian "Szabolcs de Vajay" list Fressende as the daughter of  https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-I-the-Fearless-Duke-of-Normandy/6000000010211396295. There is NO evidence that he had a daughter called 
2 CONC Fressenda/Fredesende. 
2 CONT -------
