2 CONT 14.      TANCRED de Hauteville.  Malaterra names "…sextus Tancredus…" sixth among the sons of Tancred & his second wife[265].  The Annals of Romoald name "Tancredus" as ninth son[266].  There seems no way of deciding which of thes
2 CONC e versions may be correct. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT From < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tancred_of_Hauteville ''Wikipedia''] > Accessed 20 May 2025
2 CONT
2 CONT Tancred of Hauteville (c. 980 –1041) was an 11th-century Norman lord.  Little is known about him, and he is best remembered by the achievements of his twelve sons. Various legends arose about Tancred, but they have no supporting c
2 CONC ontemporary evidence that has survived the ages.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married twice.  With his second wife, Fressenda,[7] he had at least eight more sons and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 6.   '''Tancred'''[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
