2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfralaoncou.htm#MabileRoucyMHuguesPuisetJaffa
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         MABILE de Roucy (-after 1122).  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Wiscardus et Thomas et Hugo congnomento Cholez et filie" as children of "Ebalo comite de Roceio", specifying that one daughter (unnamed, ment
2 CONC ioned first) married "Hugoni de Puisat" by whom she had "Hugonem de Gata"[431].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the wife of "Hugoni de Puisato" as sister of "Wichardum de Rocheio et comitem Hugonem Cholet"[4
2 CONC 32].  William of Tyre names the wife of Hugues du Puiset "Mamilia filia domini Hugonis Cholet comitis de Ruci[433], but it appears more acceptable chronologically for Mabile to have been the daughter of Comte Ebles II than of Comt
2 CONC e Hugues de Roucy.  William of Tyre records her marriage to "fratri comitis Namura" and his installation to succeed his wife's first husband as Lord of Jaffa[434].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly HUGUES du Puiset, son of HUGUES [I] du Puiset “Blavons” & his wife Alix de Montlhéry (-[1118]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1118/19]) ALBERT de Namur, son of ALBERT III Comte de Namur & his wife Ida von Sachsen (-before 1122).  He was installed as Lord of Jaffa in succession to his wife's first husband. 
2 CONT
