2 CONT ''  Sarno is located north-west of Salerno in the present-day Italian region of Campania.  It is recorded as a county in the 1080s, and again in the 1120s/1130s.  No information has yet been found about the county after that time.
2 CONC  ''
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#OnfroiMGaitelgrimaApulia
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.     '''    ONFROI ''' (-1081 or before).  [Conte di Sarno.  "Gaitelgrime comtesse de Sarno, veuve du comte Anfroi" is named in a charter dated 1081[784].] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' m ''' as her second husband, GAITELGRIMA of Apulia, widow of DROGO, daughter of ROBERT "Guscard" Duke of Apulia & his [second wife Sichelgaita di Salerno].  Chalandon records that Gaitelgrima, married firstly to Drogo and seco
2 CONC ndly to Onfroi, is named in a charter of Cava dated 1086[785].  "Gaitelgrime comtesse de Sarno, veuve du comte Anfroi" is named in a charter dated 1081[786].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Onfroi & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         RICHARD .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not been identified. <br>  m ---.  The name of Richard’s wife is not known.  Richard & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          RICCARDO (-after May 1125).  "Richard comte de Sarno" "filius quondam domini Riccardi qui fuit comes, ortus ex genere Normannorum" issued a charter dated Jan 1115[787].  Chalandon states that Richard made his testame
2 CONC nt dated May 1125 in the presence of his son Enrico[788]. <br> m ---.  The name of Richard’s wife is not known.  Richard & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***(a)       ENRICO (-after Jan 1138).  Chalandon states that Richard made his testament dated May 1125 in the presence of his son Enrico[789].  Conte di Sarno.  "Enrico conte di Sarno, figlio del fu conte Riccardo" donated a mill
2 CONC  to the church of Santa Maria built on the monte detto Vergine by charter dated Feb 1134[790].  "Il conte Enrico di Sarno, figlio del fu Riccardo" donated two serfs to the monastery of Montevergine by charter dated Jan 1138[791]. 
