1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTINE%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc345156292
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTINE%20NOBILITY.htm#AnnaDalassenaMIoannesKomnenos
2 CONT
2 CONT #--- Dalassena .  Her parental family is confirmed by Nikeforos Bryennios who records the marriage of "Ioanni" and "filia Charonis Alexii…Anna", stating that her mother was "genus a Dalassenis"[185].  m ALEXIOS Kharon.  Prefect of
2 CONC  Italy.  Alexios & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         ANNA Dalassena  (-1 Nov [1100/02], bur Pantopopte).  Nikeforos Bryennios records the marriage of "Ioanni" and "filia Charonis Alexii…Anna", stating that her mother was "genus a Dalassenis"[186].  The Alexeiad names "An
2 CONC na Dalassena, the mother of the Komneni" when recording that she arranged the marriage of "the grandson of Botaneiates and the daughter of Manuel her eldest son"[187].  An undated seal records “Anne Dalassène curopalatissa”[188]. 
2 CONC  Despoina 1048/57.  Regent of Byzantium 1081 and 1094-1095.  An undated seal records “Anne Dalassène la mère du basileus”[189].  She became a nun at Pantopopte convent which she founded.  The typikon of Theotokos Kecharitomenes (d
2 CONC ated to [1110]) provides for the commemoration 1 Nov of "ma...despoina, la belle-mère de ma Majesté"[190].  The list of obituaries of the monastery of Christ Philanthropos, founded by Empress Eirene Doukas, records the death 1 Nov
2 CONC  of "Annas monaxes tes metros tou basileos"[191].  m ([1042]) IOANNES Komnenos, son of MANUEL Erotikos Komnenos & his second wife --- ([1015]-12 Jul 1067).  
2 CONT
