2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Andronikos Komnenos or Andronicus Comnenus (Greek: Ανδρόνικος Κομνηνός, Andronikos Komninos, c. 1108 - 1142). Andronikos Komnenos was the third child and second son of the Byzantine Emperor John II Komnenos and his Hungarian wife,
2 CONC  Piroska (Eirene).
2 CONT
2 CONT  Life and Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Andronikos was made sebastokratōr at an unknown date. He was one of two sons of John II Komnenos to predecease that Emperor, the other being Alexios, whose body Andronikos was charged, along with the third brother, Isaac, with bri
2 CONC nging back from Attalia to Constantinople in 1142. Unfortunately, Andronikos himself became sick and died on the return journey.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Andronikos Komnenos was married to a woman named Eirene (?Aineiadissa), by whom he had several children, these were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Komnene, who married Theodoros Dasiotes, then John Kantakouzenos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Doukas Komnenos (d. c. 17 September 1176), who married (?first name unknown) Taronitissa, and had a daughter Maria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodora Komnene (d. 2 January 1184), who married Henry II Jasomirgott, and had three children, including Leopold V of Austria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudokia Komnene, who married an unknown first husband and then Michael Gabras. She was also one of the mistresses of Andronikos I Komnenos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexios Komnenos, (murd. 1183), who was married to Maria Doukaina, and had two short-lived sons. He is believed to have had Maria of Antioch (widow of Manuel I) as a mistress. He headed the regency council for her son, Alexios II.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andronikos_Komnenos_(son_of_John_II_Komnenos)
