2 CONT
2 CONT *1.        ''' daughter ([1064]-)'''.  She and her son are shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[554], but the primary source on which this is based has not been identified.  Assuming that her brother Kálmán was born in 1065, this daug
2 CONC hter must have been the older child as their mother died in [1065], the same year in which their father remarried.  The other possibility is that they were twins, which appear to have run in the family: King Kálmán's first cousin,
2 CONC  Empress Piroska [Eirene] gave birth to at least one set of twins.  m ---, from Hungary.  One child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT **a)         IVAN (-beheaded [1120/25]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   Pretender to the throne of Hungary 1120/25.  The Chronica Ungarorum records that "Bors et Juan" claimed the t
2 CONC hrone, but that "Juan" was beheaded and "Bors" sent back to Greece, dated from the context to the lifetime of István II King of Hungary[555].  
