1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://gw.geneanet.org/foullon?lang=en&pz=matheline+marie+herminia&nz=foullon&p=kotian+khan+des+kumans+kobyak&n=de+kumanie
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Notable People of Cuman Descent" / en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notable_people_of_Cuman_descent
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary -- '''Multiple contradictions are evident in this Wikipedia mini - biography.  Within the first sentence, Khan Koten is identified as "Koten Sutoiovych", thus the son of Khan Sutoi / Suthoi, but thence proceeds to ident
2 CONC ify Khan Koten as the "son of Khan Konchek".  In summary, Khan Koten / Kotian I is accurately described as the son of Khan Konchek in the second part of the sentence and inaccurately portrayed as his own grandson in the first part
2 CONC  of the sentence!! ''' That this Wikipedia mini - biography is, in fact, referencing Khan Koten / Kotian I rather than his grandson, Khan Koten / Kotian II, is attested by the accurate representation that Khan Koten / Kotian I was
2 CONC  the father in law of Kievan Rus' Knyaz Mstislav Mstislavich (1153 - 1258) by virtue of his daughter's marriage to said Knyaz Mstislav............In "WikiTree", Khan Koten / Kotian I is captioned as "Kotak of Polowzes", said to ha
2 CONC ve been born 1160 in "Polowzes, Poland" and to have died in 1240.  While the birth and death dates are consistent with those of Khan Koten / Kotian I, the location of "Polowzes, Poland" is a cipher.  "Polowzes" would appear to be 
2 CONC a Polish rendition of "Polovtsi", an alternative name for the Cumans frequently used by the  Kievan Rus'.   The daughter of "Kotak of Polowzes", Maria Kotjanovna  (i.e. daughter of Kotja / Kotak) of Novgorod, is said to have been 
2 CONC born in "Polowzes, Poland" in 1180.  Inasmuch as western Ukrainia was a part of greater Poland in later centuries, "Polowzes, Poland" would appear to be an ex post facto reference to the steppes of western Ukrainia rather than a s
2 CONC pecific urban settlement.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
