2 CONC he Oghuz, Suleiman-Shah went to Khwarazm Shah, who married him to the daughter of his brother Aqsis.[2] The couple had a son, who was named Sanjar." Reference [2] is found on page 77 of Ibn Al-Athir's ''The Chronicle of Ibn Al-Ath
2 CONC ir for the Crusading Period from Al-Kamil Fi'l-Ta'rikh,'' published in 2010. Ann K.S. Lambton states that she is Khwarazam Shah's daughter.
