2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_II_of_Duklja Vladimir II]''' (Serbian Cyrillic: Владимир; died 1118) was King of Duklja (southern parts of present-day Montenegro and northwestern parts of present-day Albania) from 1103 
2 CONC to 1113. He was a son of prince Vladimir, the oldest son of King Mihailo I of Duklja (r. 1050–1081), and thus a nephew of King Constantine Bodin (r. 1081–1101). He married a daughter of Vukan, the Grand Prince of Serbia, thereby e
2 CONC nding rivalries between the two polities. Vladimir had been appointed the rule of Duklja by his father-in-law Vukan, after the death of his uncle, former King Kočopar, in Zahumlje. He was poisoned in 1118 on the orders of Queen-Do
2 CONC wager Jaquinta, the widow of his uncle, Constantine Bodin. Jaquinta soon appointed her son, George, to the throne.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT Duklja
2 CONT Vojislavljević dynasty
2 CONT Vukanović dynasty
2 CONT Grand Principality of Serbia
2 CONT References
