1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sama%27_al-Dawla '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sama' al-Dawla''' was the Buyid ruler of Hamadan (1021-1023 or 1024). He was the son of Shams al-Dawla.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his father's death, Sama' al-Dawla succeeded him to the governorship of that province. Only after a short reign, however, the Kakuyid ruler Muhammad ibn Rustam Dushmanziyar overran Hamadan and ended Sama' al-Dawla's rule.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
