2 CONT MOUSHEGH MAMIGONIAN
2 CONT
2 CONT In response to the treachery of Shabouh, the Armenians made
2 CONT
2 CONT an aliance with Byzantium and crowned Bab, the son of Arshag
2 CONT
2 CONT as their King. In 371 A.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Armenian attempts to drive the Persians out of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT led to the famous battle of Tzirav. The catholicos Saint
2 CONT
2 CONT Nerses and King Bab Watched the battle from Mount Nebad,
2 CONT
2 CONT where Nerses raised his hands to the heavens and prayed for
2 CONT
2 CONT an Armenian victory.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Armenian general was Moushegh Mamigonian, son of the
2 CONT
2 CONT hero Vassag; his soldiers were all young men out for
2 CONT
2 CONT revenge as they had all their relatives killed by the
2 CONT
2 CONT Persians. Like a hurricane, they drove the Persian army
2 CONT
2 CONT before them. Seeing the Armenians fighting, Shabouh said:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Fortunate indeed is the king who has an army so brave and
2 CONT
2 CONT so loyal to its leader".
2 CONT
2 CONT Moushegh Mamigonian captured Shabouh's harem, but he let
2 CONT
2 CONT them go free, saying:"We don't make war against women".
2 CONT
2 CONT Shabouh admired this gesture, and he had a golden goblet
2 CONT
2 CONT made with a white horse engraved on it. When he drank from
2 CONT
2 CONT this goblet he remembered Moushegh Mamigonian and said;"
2 CONT
2 CONT Let the Knight of the white horse drinks this wine!"
