2 CONC hter of Hugh of Arles, King of Italy, who changed her name to Eudokia after her marriage. On April 6, 945, after the fall of the Lekapenoi, Constantine VII crown his son Romanos co-emperor.[citation needed][clarification needed] W
2 CONC ith Hugh out of power in Italy and dead by 947, and Bertha herself dying in 949, Romanos secured the promise from his father that he would be allowed to select his own bride. Romanos' choice fell on an innkeeper's daughter named A
2 CONC nastaso, whom he married in 956 and renamed Theophano.
2 CONT
