2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p9/4273/8120/534448379e99ab1c/Basilios_II_original.jpg?hash=aaeae1a4dd0dd06ed80afd202136c445a4ec656bc3c3e26041f86ff8e29a28ee.1797148799
2 FORM jpg
1 NOTE Basil II was but an infant when his father Romanus II died.  Basil inherited the kingdom of the Eastern Roman Empire, and was under the Regency of his mother Theophano, then when she married General Nicephorus Phokas, under their 
2 CONC guardianship until  Nicephorus died in 969.  Then  under John Tzimisces, his uncle. until 976.  Basil II then ruled until 1025 as joint emperor with his brother Constantine VIII. Basil II died in 1025, succeeded by Constantine VII
2 CONC I..
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT       Occupation:  Emperor in Byzantium
1 NOTE Served as king and lived a very long life despite his battling against rebellions and the Moors. Was more intgerested in war than in ruling his country. He was a great general because he ate the same food that his soldiers did and
2 CONC  he adopted and took care of dead soldier's orphans.
2 CONT Died childless.
2 CONT The Oxford Dictionary of Byzantium: Oxford Univ Press 1991.
2 CONT Michael Psellus, Chronographia, New Haven: Yale University Press, 1953 Vol 1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT http://www.fordam.edu/halsall/basis/psellus-chrono-02.html
1 NOTE Basil II (958?-1025), Byzantine emperor (976-1025), the greatest ruler of 
2 CONT the Macedonian dynasty. The son of Emperor Romanus II (939-63), he reigned 
2 CONT jointly with his brother Constantine VIII (960?-1028) after the death of 
2 CONT the usurper John I Tzimisces in 976, but Constantine never took an active 
2 CONT role in government. Basil's greatest achievements were the conquest of 
2 CONT Armenia in the east and the destruction of the Bulgarian Empire, which 
2 CONT threatened Byzantium on the west. He waged war on the Bulgars for nearly 
2 CONT two decades. Defeating (1014) the Bulgarian czar Samuel (flourished 
2 CONT 976-1014), he subjected his people to Byzantine rule and was given the 
2 CONT surname Bulgaroctonos (Slayer of Bulgars). The Byzantine Empire began to 
2 CONT decline after Basil's death.
