1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vsevolod Vladimirovich (983/984 - bef. 1013), prince of Volhynia, son of St. Vladimir and Rogneda of Polotsk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born between 983-984. From father received the Duchy of Volhynia, with its center in Vladimir. This city was first mentioned in 989. D. Likhachev supported Brown's hypothesis about the identity of Vsevolod with Vissavald, whom Sig
2 CONC rid the Proud burned in a bathhouse. Brown believed that the Varangian environment incited the boy to break with his father and took him to Sweden. By that time, Vsevolod could have been 11-12 years old. Voitovich considers Brown'
2 CONC s version unlikely.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 988, Kyiv Prince Vladimir Svyatoslavich conquered a city called Lodomer on the lands of the Volhynians and Buzhans on the right bank of the Luga River. And in 988 he named it after himself - Vladimir and gave the city to one of
2 CONC  his sons - Vsevolod to reign. Near Vladimir was with. Varyazh, where the army sent with the young prince was stationed.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1008 or 1013, when Volyn entered the possession of the Turov prince Svyatopolk Vladimirovich, Vsevolod was no longer alive.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Russia Rurikid:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT VSEVOLOD Vladimirovich (-1015).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Primary Chronicle names (in order) Izyaslav, Mstislav, Yaroslav, and Vsevolod as the four sons of Vladimir & his wife Rogned. The Primary Chronicle in another section names (in order) Vysheslav, Izyaslav, Yaroslav, Svyatopolk,
2 CONC  Vsevolod, Svyatoslav, Mstislav, Boris, Gleb, Stanislav, Pozvizd, and Sudislav as the twelve sons of Vladimir, recording that his father established Vsevolod in Vladimir after the death of his brother Vysheslav.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince of Volynia and Pereyaslavl 990.
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre records that Vsevolod proposed marriage to Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty", widow of Erik King of Sweden, adding that she ordered his murder in [995]
2 CONT
