2 CONT
2 CONT The Obotrites were a confederation of Western Slavic tribes in what is now northern Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estrid or Astrid of the Obotrites (ca. 979 – 1035), was married to Olof Skötkonung, the King of Sweden, ca. 1000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legend say Estrid was taken back to Sweden as a war-price; she was most likely given by her father, a chieftain of the Polabian Obotrites, as a peace offering in a marriage to seal the peace, and the guess is that she brought a gr
2 CONC eat dowry, as a great Slavic influence is represented in Sweden from her time, mainly among craftsmen. Her husband also had a mistress, Edla, who came from the same area in Europe as herself and who was perhaps taken to Sweden at 
2 CONC the same time, and the king treated Edla and Estrid the same way and gave his son and two daughters with Edla the same privilegies as the children he had with Estrid, though it was Estrid he married and made queen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Estrid was baptised with her husband, their children and large parts of the Swedish court in 1008, when the Swedish royal family converted to Christianity, though the king promised to respect the freedom of religion - Sweden
2 CONC  was not to be Christian until the last religion war of 1084-1088.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT She had a brother. She had a half-brother and a half-sister, named The Old and Astrid
