2 CONT
2 CONT Nako	954–966	Nako and his brother Stoigniew were defeated at the Raxa river (955) by Otto I, after which Stoigniew was beheaded and Nako accepted Christianity, resulting in thirty years of peace.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mstivoj and Mstidrag	966–995	Sons of Nako. They abandoned Christianity and revolted against the Germans (Great Slav Rising).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mieceslas III	919–999	in 995 defeated by Otto III, Holy Roman Emperor.
2 CONT
