2 CONT ---------
2 CONT Oda Von Stade (*cca 1040-) & Sviatoslav II Yaroslavich (*1027 -+1076)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Oda von Babenberg? Parents uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably not Vladimir’s wife. Oda’s mother was daughter of a brother of emperor Heinrich III by a sister of pope Leo IX. If Oda were their daughter, she would have been "filia germani imperatoris Henrici" indeed! The problem howev
2 CONC er is that Vladimir most probably never married this girl. The identity of his wife is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage is widely given (see http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~greenefamily/lape/pafg36.htm), but the dates appear impossible (Oda is said to have been born 1023). Could be a different Oda, of course, or a different Vl
2 CONC adimir.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Annales Stadenses name "Odam sanctimonialem de Rinthelen" as daughter of "Lippoldo filio domiine Glismodis" and "Ida [de Elsthorpe]", specifying that she married "regi Ruzie" by whom she had a son "Warteslaw", returned to Saxo
2 CONC ny with her son after her husband died, and there was mother of "filiam Aliarinam, matrem comitis Burchardi de Lucken" who later killed "lantgravius Hermannus de Wincenburg", although a later passage specifies that Ida was mother 
2 CONC of "Akarinam matrem Burchardi de Lucken”.  It has not been possible to verify this. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#VladimirIaroslavichdied1052 Medlands]
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Vladimir´s wife is not known.  Baumgarten identifies the wife of Vladimir as Oda, daughter of Luitpold Graf von Stade & his wife Ida von Elstorf [Brunswick]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grafschaft_Stade
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Wichmann d. Ä. (Billunger), † wohl 944, ? Graf an der Unterelbe
2 CONT Wichmann d. J. (Billunger), † 967, ? Graf an der Unterelbe, Sohn von Wichmann d. Ä.
2 CONT Heinrich I. der Kahle, † nach 975, Graf in Harsefeld und Legat, (Sohn von Graf Lothar (X 929)?)
2 CONT Heinrich II. der Gute, † 1016, Graf in Harsefeld, Gründer des Stifts Harsefeld, Sohn von Heinrich I.
2 CONT Siegfried, 1016 – † 1037 (?) Graf in Harsefeld, später evtl. auch in Stade, Bruder von Heinrich dem Guten
2 CONT Lothar Udo I., † 1057 Graf von Stade, ab 1056 auch Markgraf der Nordmark, Sohn von Siegfried
2 CONT Lothar Udo II., † 1082, Graf von Stade und Markgraf der Nordmark, Sohn von Lothar Udo I.
2 CONT Heinrich III. der Lange, † 1087, Graf von Stade und Markgraf der Nordmark, Sohn von Udo II.
2 CONT Lothar Udo III., † 1106, Graf von Stade und Markgraf der Nordmark, Bruder von Heinrich III.
2 CONT Rudolf I., Bruder von Lothar-Udo III., † 1124, 1106 – ca. 1115 Vormund seines Neffen Heinrich IV.
2 CONT Friedrich von Stade, ca. 1095 – 1112 Ministeriale und Vizegraf, entweder ca. 1115 durch Heinrich V. oder 1124 durch Lothar III. freigelassen, zunächst faktisch und 1128 bis † 1135 belehnter Graf von Stade
2 CONT Heinrich IV., Sohn von Lothar-Udo III., nominal ca. 1114 – † 1128 Graf von Stade, Markgraf der Nordmark
2 CONT Rudolf II. von Freckleben, Sohn von Rudolf I., 1135 – † 1144 Graf von Stade
2 CONT Hartwig, Bruder von Rudolf II., 1144/45 Dompropst in Bremen und Graf von Stade, 1148 Erzbischof von Bremen, † 1168
2 CONT Herzog Heinrich der Löwe, ab 1145 Graf von Stade
2 CONT Pfalzgraf Heinrich, Sohn Heinrichs des Löwen
