1 NOTE Henry I (of France) (circa 1008-60), king of France (1031-60), son of King 
2 CONT Robert II and grandson of Hugh Capet, founder of the Capetian dynasty. 
2 CONT From the beginning of his reign he was occupied with putting down 
2 CONT rebellions led by members of his family and other French nobles. Between 
2 CONT 1035 and 1047 he assisted his nephew William, duke of Normandy, later 
2 CONT William the Conqueror, king of England, in establishing William's 
2 CONT authority over rebellious Norman nobles. Henry later grew jealous of 
2 CONT William's power and waged unsuccessful war against him in 1054 and 1058. 
2 CONT Henry was succeeded by his son Philip I.
