1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please note that this is a son of Henry of France and Anna of Kiev that did not make it to adulthood. (Therefore it follows that he never had a wife.)
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on France Capetian Kings:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT de France (before Jun 1054-[1063]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Liber Modernorum Regum Francorum names (in order) "Philippum, Hugonem atque Rotbertum" as the three sons of King Henri & Anna, specifying that "Rotbertus inmatura morte decessit"[244].  This is confirmed by the Chronicle of Al
2 CONC beric de Trois-Fontaines which names (in order) "Philippum, Robertum et Hugonam" as the three sons of King Henri, specifying that "Robertus iuvenis mortuus est"[245].
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpted from the English Wikipedia page of his father, Henry I of France:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_I_of_France
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I married Anne of Kiev on 19 May 1051. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Philip I (23 May 1052 – 30 July 1108)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Emma (born 1054, date of death unknown)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Robert (c. 1055 – c. 1060)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Hugh the Great (1057–1102)
2 CONT
2 CONT From the corresponding French Wikipedia page:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Ier_de_France
2 CONT
2 CONT Enfants 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Philippe Ier (1052-1108)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Robert (1054-1063)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Emma (1055-1109)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Hugues (1057-1102), comte de Vermandois, époux d'Adélaïde de Vermandois.
