2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe I, Roi de France [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #103094, b. circa 1052, d. 29 July 1108
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=19 Jun 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe I, Roi de France was born circa 1052.[2] He was the son of Henri I, Roi de France and Anne of Kiev.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Berthe de Hollande, daughter of Florent I, Comte de Hollande, in 1071/72.[3] He and Berthe de Hollande were divorced in 1091.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Bertrada de Montfort, daughter of Simon de Montfort, Sire de Montfort l'Aumari and Agnes d'Evreux, in 1095. He died on 29 July 1108.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe I, Roi de France was a member of the House of Capet.[1] He succeeded to the title of Roi Philippe I de France in 1060.[4],[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe I, Roi de France also went by the nick-name of Philippe 'the Fair'.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Philippe I, Roi de France and Berthe de Hollande
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Constance de France+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. bt 1072 - 1095, d. 1125
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Louis VI, Roi de France+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 1077/78, d. 1 Aug 1137
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Philippe I, Roi de France and Bertrada de Montfort
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Philippe de France,[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 1093, d. a 1123
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Cecilia de France 
2 CONT
2 CONT b. bt 1095 - 1108
