1 NOTE Philip I (of France) (1052-1108), king of France (1060-1108), the eldest 
2 CONT son of Henry I, king of France. The first six years of his reign were 
2 CONT spent under the regency of his mother and his uncle. Philip's reign was 
2 CONT troubled by many clashes with his powerful vassals, particularly in 
2 CONT Normandy, but he succeeded in enlarging his dominions. Philip was 
2 CONT excommunicated in 1095 because he had repudiated his wife, Bertha of 
2 CONT Holland, and married Bertrada, the wife of the count of Anjou.
1 NOTE KING OF FRANCE 1060-1108 (BECAME KING 8/4/1060); POSSIBLY DIED OF MALARIA
1 NOTE Philip I (1052-1108), king of France, began to reign in 1060. Before his death Philip had annexed Vexin and Valois, and had purchased Bourges; he had also given Vermandois to his brother Hugh. [The Home University Encyclopedia, 19
2 CONC 46]
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE Fils aãinâe d'Henri Ier et d'Anne de Kiev, Philippe est associâe au trãone en 1059 et devient roi en 1060, áa l'ãage de huit ans, sous la râegence de son oncle Baudoin V, comte de Flandre.
2 CONT Pendant son ráegne, il intervient dans les luttes entre grands fâeodaux. Pour la succession de Flandre, apráes la mort du comte, Philippe 1er monte une expâedition, mais il est battu áa Cassel en 1071 par Robert le Frison. En 1081
2 CONC , il soutient Robert Courteheuse contre son páere Guillaume le Conquâerant, duc de Normandie et roi d'Angleterre, mais en vain.
2 CONT Il agrandit le domaine royal, avec les acquisitions du Gãatinais, du Vexin, de Corbie et de Bourges et sous son ráegne, l'autoritâe monarchique commence áa se faire sentir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe 1er âepouse en 1071 Berthe de Hollande, mais la râepudie en 1091 pour âepouser Bertrade de Montfort, femme de Foulques d'Anjou, qu'il avait enlevâee, ce qui lui vaut l'excommunication du pape Urbain II (1094), puis l'inte
2 CONC rdit jetâe sur le royaume (1100). Mais, insoucieux des excommunications, il continu sa vie consacrâee davantage aux plaisirs qu'áa ses fonctions.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Il meurt en 1108, en ayant prâeparâe sa succession par le couronnement de son fils Louis le Gros en 1100.
1 NOTE Also had children with Bertrade De Montfort
2 CONT (not married)
2 CONT Philippe, Comte de Mantes (living 1123) 
2 CONT Fleury, seigneur de Nagis (living 1118) 
2 CONT Cecile of France, married Tancred, Prince of Galilee; married secondly Pons of Tripoli 
