2 CONT Koloman Arpád, King of Hungary was the son of Geisa I Arpád, King of Hungary and Synadene Synadenos. (1) He married, firstly, Buzilla of Sicily, daughter of Roger I, Count of Sicily, in 1097. (1) He married, secondly, Euphemia of 
2 CONC Kiev, daughter of Vladimir II Monomakh, Prince of Novgorod and Kiev and Gytha (?), in 1104. (1) He and Euphemia of Kiev were divorced in 1113. (1) 
