1 NOTE Koloman (Kalman) or Salomon, natural son of Geza II, became King of Hungary succeeding his uncle Ladislaus I in 1095.  Koloman or Soloman ruled until 1116, and was succeeded by Stephen II.
1 NOTE He reigned from 1095 to 1116. He was the son of Geza by a Greek concubine. He spent his youth in Poland. He returned to seize the crown when his uncle Ladislas died.
