2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopediaJump to: navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT Boris Kalamanos (Kiev, c. 1114-1153/1154) was a pretender who claimed the Hungarian throne. He desperately tried to assert his claims with the assistance of Poland, the Holy Roman Empire and the Byzantine Empire, but he failed and
2 CONC  died in exile.
2 CONT
