1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vasilko Yurievich''' (d. after 1161) - Prince of Suzdal (1149-1151), Poross (1155-1161), son of Yuri Dolgorukiy.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the approval of Yuri Dolgorukiy on the Kiev grand prince's throne in 1149, Vasilko was appointed his governor in Suzdal. After the final approval of Yuri in Kyiv (1155), he did not plant one of his sons in Suzdal, and soon A
2 CONC ndrey Yuryevich left Vyshgorod for Vladimir. After the death of his father (1157), Vasilko held out in the south until 1161 (then, with the participation of Vasilko and the black hoods, Izyaslav Davydovich died in the struggle for
2 CONC  the Kievan reign). Then, together with other relatives, Andrey was sent to Byzantium, where he managed some possessions on the Danube. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Vasilko was the founder of Vasileva Sloboda (the modern city of Chkalovsk).
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no information about Vasilko's family and descendants.
