1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert I of Capua
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopediaJump to: navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert I (died 1120), count of Aversa and prince of Capua from 1106, on the death of his elder and heirless brother Richard, was the second eldest son of Jordan I of Capua and Gaitelgrima, daughter of Guaimar IV of Salerno.
2 CONT
2 CONT He tried to be the papal protector which his father and grandfather had been and he sent three hundred knights to rescue Pope Paschal II and his sixteen cardinals during their imprisonment by Emperor Henry V in 1111. However, his 
2 CONC troops were turned back by the count of Tusculum, Ptolemy I, and never made it to their goal.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1114, he and Jordan of Ariano assaulted papal Benevento, but the Archbishop Landulf II made peace with them.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1117, Paschal fled to him and he hosted his successor, Gelasius II, later in 1118, even escorting him back to Rome with his army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Though he did not recognise the Apulian suzerainty which his brother had been forced to acknowledge, he was nonetheless a petty and secondary power in the Mezzogiorno. He died in 1120, leaving a son and successor in the infant Ric
2 CONC hard III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_I_of_Capua
