2 CONT 2.         JEAN ([1108/11]-Apulia [1115/20]).  Fulcher of Chartres records that Prince Bohémond and Constance "duos filios habuit", specifying that Bohémond was the older son[39].  Suger's Vita Ludovici records that "Antiochenum p
2 CONC rincipem Boamundum" & his wife had two sons (in order) "Johannem et Boamundum", and specifies that Jean died in Apulia "ante annos militiæ"[40]. 
