2 CONT 2.         GUILLAUME ([1070/75]-killed in battle Dorylæum, Asia Minor 1 Jul 1097).  He is called "Guillelmus marchisi filius" by Orderic Vitalis, who states that he embarked at Bari in [1096/97] as part of the First Crusade with H
2 CONC ugues Comte de Vermandois and sailed to Durazzo where they were arrested by the city's governor and sent to the emperor at Constantinople[80].   His birth date range is estimated from the likely birth date range of his sister, the
2 CONC  likely date of their parents' marriage, and Guillaume being described by Albert of Aix as "iuvenis…tiro" when he died.  Baudry calls him "Guillelmus Marchisus, Tancred frater" when recording his death[81], which suggests that he 
2 CONC had inherited the title "Marquis" from his father and that he was therefore the older brother.  William of Tyre specifies that he was the brother of Tancred when he reports his death at the battle of Dorylaeum against the Turks[82
2 CONC ].  Albert of Aix calls him "Willelmus iuvenis audacissimus, tiro pulcherrimus, frater Tancredi" when recording his death[83]. 
