2 CONT 2.         BEATRIX de Hauteville ([1005/10]-1101).  The Annals of Romoald state that Tancred had three daughters without naming them or stating by which marriage they were born[90].  The chronology of her descendants strongly sugg
2 CONC ests that Beatrix must have been born in [1005/10] and therefore was one of her parents' older children.  The primary source which confirms her name and two marriages has not yet been identified.  Beatrix is shown as the daughter 
2 CONC of Tancred by his first wife in Europäische Stammtafeln[91].  The basis for this is not known.  However, it appears more likely that she was the daughter of his second marriage if her estimated birth date range is correct, especia
2 CONC lly in light of the approximate date of birth of her brother Robert "Guiscard" in [1020].  The Gesta Roberti Wiscardi names "Robertus de Scabioso Monte comes…Gosfredi frater, et ambo orti germana fuerant ducis"[92].  Guerrieri hig
2 CONC hlights that "Gosfredi" in this passage has been identified as Godefroi Conte di Conversano but that it is not possible to confirm whether this is correct[93].  If the speculation is right, Beatrix was the same person as the daugh
2 CONC ter of Tancred who is shown below as married to "--- [di Conversano]".  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ARMAND de Mortain, son of ROBERT Comte d'Eu [Normandie] & his first wife Béatrice ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ROGER, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT - - - - - - - - - - - - - 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         [daughter .  The Annals of Romoald state that Tancred had three daughters without naming them or stating by which marriage they were born[238].  If Orderic Vitalis is correct in saying that "Geoffroy di Conversano" was 
2 CONC nepos of Robert "Guiscard" Duke of Apulia, his mother must have been the Duke's sister[239].  This is confirmed when Malaterra records that "Gaufridum de Conversano neptem suis [Roberti ducis]…filius…sororis suæ"[240].  The Gesta 
2 CONC Roberti Wiscardi names "Robertus de Scabioso Monte comes…Gosfredi frater, et ambo orti germana fuerant ducis"[241].  Guerrieri highlights that "Gosfredi" in this passage has been identified as Godefroi Conte di Conversano but that
2 CONC  it is not possible to confirm whether this is correct[242].  If the speculation is right, this daughter was the '''same person as [Beatrix]''', wife of Armand de Mortain (see above).  
2 CONT
