2 CONT 2.         RICCARDO ([1053/60]-Spring 1112[503]).  William of Tyre records "Richardus de Principatu filius Guillelmi Ferrebrachia[504] fratris Roberti Guischart, Ranulfus frater eius" among those who accompanied Bohemond on the Fi
2 CONC rst Crusade in 1097[505], although the reference to "…Guillelmi Ferrebrachia…" must be incorrect resulting from confusion in the source between the two brothers of Robert "Guiscard" who were both called Guillaume.  "Ricardus de Pr
2 CONC incipatu et Ranulfus frater eius" are also recorded by Orderic Vitalis on the same occasion[506].  Albert of Aix records that "Richardus princeps Salernæ civitatis Italiæ de genere Nortmannorum, proximus Tancredi" was captured dur
2 CONC ing the siege of Mamistra, dated to late 1097 from the context[507].  "Ricardo de Principatu filiolo di Roberto Ferra Brachiu fratel di Roberto Guiscardo" is recorded in Itinerario di la Gran Militia a la Pavese[508].  According t
2 CONC o Europäische Stammtafeln[509], Richard was the son of Drogo de Hauteville Count of Apulia.  His birth date is estimated from the likely marriage date of his parents.  Vardan's History records that "Danishman lord of Sebastia, who
2 CONC m they say was of Armenian nationality, came against Melitene" in 1100 and captured "Pemond and Rajard who were at Edessa [and] who came against him"[510]: it is suggested that "Rajard" was Richard of the Principate.  He was appoi
2 CONC nted regent in Edessa in 1104 during the captivity of Baudouin II Count of Edessa[511], but Baudouin had to evict him forcibly to regain Edessa in 1108 after his release in 1107[512].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ALTRUDE, daughter of Marchese ODO [Guglielmo] "le Bon" & his wife Emma of Apulia.  Albert of Aix records the mother of Roger Prince of Antioch as the sister of Tancred, but does not name her[513].  The primary source which
2 CONC  confirms her name has not yet been identified.  If the estimated birth date of her son is correct, Altrude could not have been born later than [1065/70].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[514], Richard's wife was Altrude, dau
2 CONC ghter of Godofredo Conte di Conversano e Brindisi, but this is inconsistent with Tancred regent of Antioch having appointed his nephew, Richard's son Roger, as his heir. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        PRINCES of ANTIOCH.    
