2 CONC onis domini Sergii…consul et dux atque…magister militum et imperialis protosevasto et quondam domina Limpiasa…ducissa que fuit filia quondam vone memorie domini Riccardi principis Capuane civitatis iugalium personarum" exchanged p
2 CONC roperty with the monastery of SS Sergio & Bacchio[1828].  It appears more acceptable from a chronological point of view that she was the daughter of Richard I Prince of Capua than Richard II.  Stasser suggests that the marriage to
2 CONC ok place after her father died, marking the end of the siege of Naples[1829].  
