2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SICILY.htm#Rogerdied1101B
2 CONT
2 CONT ([1063]-after Aug 1119).  Malaterra names "filiam eius…Emmam…de prima uxore Judicta" when recording that her father arranged her marriage to Philippe I King of France, in return for a generous dowry, not knowing that the king was 
2 CONC still married to Bertha of Holland.  She left for France, but when the king's marital status came to light, the dowry was sent back to Sicily and her marriage to the Comte de Clermont was arranged by her brother-in-law Raymond de 
2 CONC Saint-Gilles[410].  "Radulfus Machabeus…Montis Scaviosi dominus" donated property, for the souls of "domini patris mei Umfredi et fratris mei Gosfredi et…Iordanis cognati mei…dominæ matris meæ Beatricis…et domine Judettæ socrus me
2 CONC æ…coniugis meæ dominæ Emmæ…Adeliciæ sororis meæ", by charter dated May 1099[411].  "Emma comitissa…civitatis Severiane" donated property, for the souls of "viri mei domini Radulfi Machabei nostrorum filiorum", by charter dated Sep
2 CONC  1110, subscribed by "Rogerius civitatis Severiane dominus et filii Rodulfi Machabei Emme comitisse, Emma comitisse comitis Rogerii filiæ…"[412].  Pope Pascal II confirmed the possessions of the abbey of Notre-Dame de Josaphat in 
2 CONC Sicily and Calabria by charter dated 3 Jan 1113, listing the donations including "Emme filie Rogerii comitis Sicilie et Calabrie…orto ante ecclesiam Sancte Perpetue"[413].  "Emma comitissa Rogerii comitis filia civitatis Severiane
2 CONC  domina" donated property to "monasterio sancti Michaelis archangeli", for "me et viri mei Randulfi Machabei nostrorum filiorum", by charter dated 1115, subscribed by "domini Rogerii Machabei prescripte comitisse filii, domine Ade
2 CONC licze iamdicte comitisse filie…"[414].  "Emma comitissa Rogerii comitis filia civitatis Severiane domina…cum filio meo domino Rogerio Machabeo" donated property to "sancte Trinitatis…domus hospitalis" by charter dated Jul 1119[415
2 CONC ].  "Emma comitissa Rogerii comitis filia civitatis Severiane domina…cum filio meo domino Rogerio Machabeo" donated property to "domus hospitalis Sancti Iohannis Iherosolomitani" by charter dated Aug 1119[416].  "Rogerius…Sicilie 
2 CONC et Italie rex" confirmed donations "a beate memorie Emma sorore nostra quondam comitissa civitate Severiane et Appii domina" to the church of St Basilius in Appia by charter dated 21 Sep 1133[417].  "Rogerius…Sicilie et Italie rex
2 CONC …Rogerii primi comitis heres et filius" confirmed past donations to St Mary Josephat, Jerusalem by (among others) "dna Emma soror nostra uxor quondam Radulfi Machabei" by charter dated 11 Oct 1144[418].  m firstly ([1086/87], repu
2 CONC diated?) GUILLAUME [VI] Comte d'Auvergne, son of ROBERT [II] Comte d'Auvergne & his second wife Judith de Melgueil (-1136).  This first marriage is not mentioned in Europäische Stammtafeln[419] but is consistent with the story con
2 CONC cerning Emma's projected marriage with the king of France quoted above.  According to another table in Europäische Stammtafeln[420], the wife of Comte Guillaume [VI] was Emma, daughter of Guillaume d'Evreux, who was the maternal a
2 CONC unt of Emma, daughter of Count Roger, but this appears impossible chronologically.  m secondly RODOLFO MACABEO Conte di Montescaglioso, son of UNFREDO Conte di Montescaglioso [Normandie] & his wife Beatrice --- (-[1115/19]).  
