2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/JERUSALEM%20NOBILITY.htm#HuguesPuisetJaffadied1118
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT HUGUES du Puiset, son of HUGUES [I] du Puiset “Blavons” Vicomte de Chartres & his wife Alix de Montlhéry (-[1118]).  The donation of property to "sancti Petro" by "Hugo vicecomes" is recorded in a charter dated 1096, subscribed by
2 CONC  "Adelidis uxor vicecomitis, filii eorum, Ebrardus, Hugo, Guiddo et filia Unberga"[524].  Hugues arrived in Palestine after 1106 and acquired land in Jaffa.  Orderic Vitalis records that “Hugo enim de Pusacio et Simon de Aneto, Ro
2 CONC dulfus quoque de Ponte Erchenfredi et Guascelinus frater eius” accompanied Bohémond I Prince of Antioch in Apulia in 1107[525].  Baudouin I King of Jerusalem confirmed donations to the Knights Hospitallers, among which "in terra d
2 CONC e Ascalona…Casale" by "Hugo de Puzath", by charter dated 28 Sep 1110[526].  Jaffa was elevated to the status of a lordship in 1118 by Baudouin II King of Jerusalem, and Hugues was installed as Lord of Jaffa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as her first husband, MABILE de Roucy, daughter of EBLES [II] Comte de Roucy & his wife Sibylle of Apulia .  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Wiscardus et Thomas et Hugo cognomento Cholez et filie" as children
2 CONC  of "Ebalo comite de Roceio", specifying that one daughter (unnamed, mentioned first) married "Hugoni de Puisat" by whom she had "Hugonem de Gata"[527].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the wife of "Hugoni de
2 CONC  Puisato" as sister of "Wichardum de Rocheio et comitem Hugonem Cholet"[528].  William of Tyre names the wife of Hugues du Puiset "Mamilia filia domini Hugonis Cholet comitis de Ruci[529], but this appears to be incorrect.  After 
2 CONC her husband's death, she married ([1118/19]) Albert de Namur.   William of Tyre records the marriage of "fratri comitis Namura" and his installation to succeed his wife's first husband as Lord of Jaffa[530]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Hugues & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT *1.         HUGUES du Puiset (-after Jul 1134). .. ... .... ....
2 CONT
