2 CONT 4.       '''  ALBERT de Namur''' (-shortly before 1122).  The Genealogica ex Stirpe Sancti Arnulfi names (in order) "Fridericum episcopum, Godefridum, Henricum et Albertum fratres" as sons of "Albertum comitem"[85].  The Chronicle
2 CONC  of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Godefridum comitem de Namuco et comitem Albertum de Rupe et sorores eorum" as children of "Albertus comes senior Namucensis", although it appears probable that Alberic intended to refer to "He
2 CONC inricum de Rupe" instead of "Albertum" given that on a subsequent page he lists the children of "Henricum" as children of "Albertum"[86].  William of Tyre records the marriage of "fratri comitis Namura" and his installation to suc
2 CONC ceed his wife's first husband as Lord of Jaffa[87].  
2 CONT
