2 CONT ii)         GODEFROI [I] (-after 1107).  An undated charter dated records the settlement of disputes between Saint-Amand and “Anselmum [...de Bouchain]...Berta uxor Anselmi et Godefridi filius eius [...frater eius], et Rainerus” s
2 CONC ettled disputes and their donations[641].  “Ansellus Valencen, castellan. Ribedimontis et Oestrevandie dominus” founded Anchin abbey by charter dated 1096, in the presence of “Godefridus de Ribodimonte filius meus...”[642].  "Gode
2 CONC fridus filius Anselli de Ribodimonte et Rainerus dapifer illius" donated property to "Aquicinensis cœnobii" by charter dated 1103, witnessed by "Hugo castellanus Valentianensis…"[643].  Châtelain de Valenciennes.  “Godefridus fili
2 CONC us Anselli de Ribodimonte et Rainerus dapifer ipsius” confirmed donations, for the soul of “memorati Anselli...Aquicinensis cœnobii fundator”, by charter dated 1103, witnessed by “Hugo castellanus Valentianensis...”[644].  Godefro
2 CONC i de Ribemont, son of Anselme, confirmed his father's last wishes by two charters dated 1104[645].  “Gerardus [error for Godefridus] Anselmi filius de Ribodimonte” confirmed donations to Ribemont Saint-Nicolas made by “pater meus 
2 CONC Anselmus” by charter dated 1104, subscribed by “Godefridi comitis...”[646].  "Godefridi, Hugonis, castellanorum de Valentianis…" signed the charter dated 1107 under which "Emmissa quæ cognominor comitissa, Isaac et Maltheldis fili
