1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Maria Komnene''', who married Theodoros Dasiotes, then John Kantakouzenos.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andronikos_Komnenos_(son_of_John_II)#Family
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2010571204.htm#MariaKborn1126
2 CONT
2 CONT a)       '''  MARIA Komnene''' ( [1126]- ).  Niketas Choniates names "Alexius, Andronicus et…Isaacius" as the three brothers of Emperor Manuel, stating that Andronikos left daughters "Mariam, Theodoram et Eudociam"[297].  Niketas 
2 CONC Choniates names "Maria…Andronici sebastocrator…filia" as wife of "Dasiotes"[298].  Her second marriage is indicated by Ioannes Kinnamos who records that "Ioannes cognomento…Cantacuzenus" married "Andronici sebastocratoris filiam"[
2 CONC 299].  As the marriages of Maria's known sisters Theodora and Evdokia are recorded in other sources (see below), it is assumed that Kinnamos is referring to a second marriage of Maria in this passage, unless Andronikos Komnenos ha
2 CONC d a fourth daughter who is otherwise unrecorded.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (1139) THEODOROS Dasiotes, son of --- (-Iconium [1143/44]).  He died in prison.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1145/50]) IOANNES Kantakouzenos, son of --- Kantakouzenos & his wife --- (-killed in battle Myriokephalon 17 Sep 1176).  Pansébastos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
