2 CONT MANUEL Komnenos, son of Emperor IOANNES II & his wife [Piroska] [Eirene] of Hungary (Constantinople [15 Aug 1118]-24 Sep 1180, bur Monastery of Christ Pantocrator[404]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Betrothed ([1159/60]) to MELISENDE of Tripoli, daughter of RAYMOND II Count of Tripoli [Toulouse] & his wife Hodierne of Jerusalem (-after 1162).  Ioannes Kinnamos records that "Ioannem Contostephanum sebastum et Theophylactum vir
2 CONC um Italum" were sent to negotiate a marriage with "puella Tripoli in Phoenicia, gente quidem Latina"[420].  She was nominated by Baudouin III King of Jerusalem in 1159 as a prospective bride when the emperor asked the king to choo
2 CONC se a wife for him from among the princesses of Outremer.  However, Manual repudiated the betrothal in [Jul] 1161, apparently after being told that there were doubts about Mélisende's legitimacy based on her mother's known quarrel 
2 CONC with her father[421]. 
