2 CONT
2 CONT 3.       '''  [MARIA Komnene''' (before 1160-).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.  Hannick & Schmalzbauer record that “Theodoros Synadenos” married “der Tochter des Andronikos I
2 CONC . Komnenos, Maria”[489].  However, in the same paragraph they confuse this Maria with Maria, daughter of Andronikos Komnenos sébastokrator and his wife Eirene [Aineiadissa], in consequence stating that Theodoros Synadenos must hav
2 CONC e died before 1143 in view of the supposed second marriage of his widow.  It is therefore unclear whether there is doubt about the identity of this daughter of Emperor Andronikos.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after 1184) THEODOROS Synadenos, son of ---.] 
