2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Hungary 
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Bernardo and Salem Maragone, Annales Pisani pp. 68-9 Gentile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Letter of Alexander III to Archbishop Henry of Reims, 28 February 1171 (Patrologia Latina vol. 200 column 783). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Annales Pisani; Ottobono, Annales Genuenses, 1179. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ W. Regel, Fontes rerum byzantinicarum (St Petersburg, 1892-1917) p. 84. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ For references see Alexios II Komnenos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ For example, Irene Doukaina, wife to Alexios I Komnenos and paternal grandmother to Manuel, was twelve years old at her marriage in 1078. Theodora Komnene, niece of Manuel and Queen consort of Baldwin III of Jerusalem, was thirt
2 CONC een years old at her marriage in 1158. Margaret of Hungary would marry Isaac II Angelos in 1185 when she was approximately ten years old, but this was an exceptional case, Isaac in 1185 being far from secure in his hold on power a
2 CONC nd having an urgent need for dynastic support. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ William of Tyre, Historia Transmarina 22.4; Roger of Howden, Chronicle, year 1180. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Madrid MS Esc. Gr. 265 [Y.II.10] fols 368-372 (as described in G. de Andrés, Catálogo de los códices griegos de la Real Biblioteca de El Escorial Vol. 2 [Madrid, 1965] pp. 120-131). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ For details, with references to sources, see Maria of Antioch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Niketas Choniates, Histories p. 347 van Dieten. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Alberic of Trois-Fontaines, Chronicle 1193. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Alberic of Trois-Fontaines, Chronicle 1204. According to the Crusade memoir of Robert of Clari they were already married; however, Alberic's information appears more soundly based. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Alberic of Trois-Fontaines, Chronicle 1205 and 1235. 
2 CONT
