1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theodore Kastamonites was Euphrosyne's brother and NOT her husband. ref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Kastamonites Theodore was the brother of Euphrosyne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Euphrosyne was the wife of Andronikos Doukas Angelos (and Alexios III Angelos), and mother of the emperors Isaac II Angelos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Euphrosyne and Alexios III Angelos died in Arta, Greece in the year 1211-1212). Alexios III Angelos (c. 1153 – 1211), raised to sebastokrator by his brother Isaac II Angelos, usurped the throne from him in 1195. Generally an inept
2 CONC  and pleasure-loving ruler, he reigned until he fled before the attacks of the Fourth Crusade happening in the year1203. He tried to capture the Empire of Nicaea in the year 1211, but was defeated by Theodore I Laskaris and died s
2 CONC oon after (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphrosyne_Doukaina_Kamatera)
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodoros Kastamonites is NOT Euphrosyne*s father. Please read biological father as: Andronikos Doukas Kamateros, Duke of the Byzantine Empire.  Born ca 1108 in Constantinople, died 1176.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife I. Theodora Kalusine Kantakouzene and maybe the very young biological mother of Euphrosyne.  According to official data Theodora Kalusine and her sister, Anna Komnene is the half-sister of Alexios III Angelos with the same fa
2 CONC ther Konstantine Angelos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife II: Qirwerne, Princess of Ethiopia, B ca. 1099, D 1159
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00049873&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT https://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I960&tree=EuropeRoyalNobleHous
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euphrosyne_Doukaina_Kamatera
2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT Vivió entre (c.1125-1190), hija de Teodoro Kastamounites. Casó antes de 1155 con Andronikos Dukas Angelos, que nació hacia el año 1122, en Constantinopla, Bizancio. Murió el 2-XII-1185. Tuvieron por hijos a: 1) Juan (príncipe de B
2 CONC izancio), 2) Alexios III (emperador de Bizancio, e 3) Isaac II Angelos, emperador de Bizancio, que nació, en Constantinopla, hacia 1156. Murió el 28-I-1202/1203, ejecutado. Casó con Irene Comnene.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Isaac II Angelos From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Andronikos Dukas Angelos, a military leader in Asia Minor (c. 1122 – aft. 1185), married bef. 1155 Euphrosyne Kastamonitissa (c. 1125 – aft. 1195), was a son of Theodora Komnene (b. January 5, 1096/1097), the youngest daughter of 
2 CONC Emperor Alexios I Komnenos and Eirene Doukaina, by her marriage c. 1120 to Konstantinos Angelos, Admiral of Sicily (c. 1085 – aft. July 1166)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Alexios III Angelos From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexios III Angelos was the second son of Andronicos Angelos and Euphrosyne Castamonitissa. Andronicus was himself a son of Theodora Comnene, the youngest daughter of Emperor Alexios I Komnenos and Irene Ducaena.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Euphrosyne Kastamonitissa married Andronikos Dukas Angelos sometime before 1155. She died sometime after 1195.
