1 NOTE Boris II of Bulgaria's First Kingdom, the son of Peter I, reigned from 969 to 972.  His country was invaded by Svyatoslav, who then became master of the country.  In turn, Emperor John Zimisces of the Byzantine Empire claimed Bulg
2 CONC aria, and abolished the Bulgarian patriarchate, and the country was then ruled by Byzantine garrisons throughout.  Samuel or Samuil, son of Nicholas Shishman, a nobleman, took over after Boris II.  This ended the dynasty of the Ko
2 CONC rmisosh and Kubrat reign of Bulgaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Boris II of Bulgaria, great grandson of Romanus Lecapenus of the Byzantine Empire, invaded the Balkans in 971.  The Byzantine General John Tzimisces, surround the army of Boris, captured him, and made him prisoner in Constantinopl
2 CONC e.  Boris II was then deposed in 972, and forced to abdicate.
