2 CONT 4.          BERTA ([927/30]-Autumn 949).  Liutprand specifies that the wife of Romanos was the illegitimate daughter of King Ugo, "the Greeks not enquiring about the nobility of her mother"[729], and in a later passage names her B
2 CONC erta "filiam suam quam ex meretrice Pezola ipse genuerat" specifying that she was called EVDOKIA in Byzantium[730].  Theophanes Continuatus records the marriage in Sep of "Hugonem regem Franciæ…filiam" and "Romanus imperator…Roman
2 CONC o Constantini generi sui filio", stating that she lived five years with her husband[731], which confuses the identity of Berta's father.  Cedrenus records that "filia Hugonis", married to "Romano", died a virgin[732].  
2 CONT
