1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grand Prince Vladimir had nine illegitimate children by unknown Mistresses (3) to (9): 
2 CONT 11.       GLEB Vladimirovich (-murdered 5 Sep 1015, bur Lto river, transferred 1072 to Vishgorod[136]).  The Primary Chronicle names (in order) Vysheslav, Izyaslav, Yaroslav, Sviatopolk, Vsevolod, Sviatoslav, Mstislav, Boris, Gleb
2 CONC , Stanislav, Pozvizd and Sudislav as the twelve sons of Vladimir, recording that his father established Gleb in Murom after the death of his brother Vysheslav[137].  His father appointed him Prince of Murom in 1010.  He was lured 
2 CONC by deceit from Murom and murdered on the orders of his cousin Sviatopolk I Grand Prince of Kiev[138].  He was canonised with his brother Boris in 1072. 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%B1_%D0%92%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87_%28%D0%BA%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%B7%D1%8C_%D0%BC%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9%29
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#VladimirIdied1015
2 CONT
2 CONT VLADIMIR I 980-1015, SVIATOPOLK I 1015-1019
2 CONT
2 CONT VLADIMIR Sviatoslavich, son of SVIATOSLAV I Grand Prince of Kiev & his mistress Malusha [Malfred] ([960]-Berestov 15 Jul 1015).
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([977], divorced 986) as her second husband, ROGNED of Polotsk, widow of --- Jarl in Sweden, daughter of ROGVOLOD Prince of Polotsk & his wife --- ([956]-[998/1000]).
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (Kherson 988) ANNA of Byzantium, daughter of Emperor ROMANOS II & his second wife Theophano [née Anastasia] (963-[1008/11], bur Kiev, church of the Palace).
2 CONT
2 CONT m thirdly (after 1011) [ADELIA] [von Öhningen, daughter of KONRAD Duke of Swabia & his wife Richlint ---] (-after 14 Aug 1018).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (1): ---, wife of IAROPOLK Sviatoslavich, daughter of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (2): OLAVA, a Czech concubine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistresses (3) to (9): ---.  The names of the other mistresses of Grand Prince Vladimir are not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince Vladimir & his first wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.             IZIASLAV Vladimirovich (-1001).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.             IAROSLAV Vladimirovich ([978]-20 Feb 1054).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.             MSTISLAV Vladimirovich "the Brave" (978-[1034/36], bur Church of the Redeemer).
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.             VSEVOLOD Vladimirovich (-1015).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.             daughter (-after 1018).
2 CONT
2 CONT ... same person as…?  PREDSLAVA Vladimirovna (-after 1018).
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Predslava married Boleslav III Duke of the Bohemians.
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.             daughter (-after 1018).  The Primary Chronicle records that Vladimir and his wife Rogned had two unnamed daughters[106].  The Primary Chronicle records that Boleslav of Poland fled from Kiev in 1018 with Iaroslav's 
2 CONC two sisters[107].
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince Vladimir had one illegitimate son by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.              SVIATOPOLK Vladimirovich ([980]-1019).
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince Vladimir had one illegitimate son by Mistress (2):
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.              VYSHESLAV Vladimirovich (-1010).
2 CONT
2 CONT Grand Prince Vladimir had nine illegitimate children by unknown Mistresses (3) to (9):
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.              SVIATOSLAV Vladimirovich (-killed in battle 1015 after 15 Jul).
2 CONT
2 CONT 10.           BORIS Vladimirovich ([990]-murdered 24 Jul 1015, bur Lto river, transferred 1072 to Vishgorod
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.           GLEB Vladimirovich (-murdered 5 Sep 1015, bur Lto river, transferred 1072 to Vishgorod[125]).  The Primary Chronicle names (in order) Vysheslav, Izyaslav, Yaroslav, Svyatopolk, Vsevolod, Svyatoslav, Mstislav, Boris, 
2 CONC Gleb, Stanislav, Pozvizd and Sudislav as the twelve sons of Vladimir, recording that his father established Gleb in Murom after the death of his brother Vysheslav[126].  His father appointed him Prince of Murom in 1010.  He was lu
2 CONC red by deceit from Murom and murdered on the orders of his cousin Sviatopolk I Grand Prince of Kiev[127].  He was canonised with his brother Boris in 1072.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12.           POZVIZD [Kryzokyr] Vladimirovich (-after 1015).
2 CONT
2 CONT 13.           SUDISLAV Vladimirovich (-Kiev [1062/63], bur Church of St George).
2 CONT
2 CONT 14.           STANISLAV Vladimirovich (-before 1015).
2 CONT
2 CONT 15.           [--- Vladimirovna .  ... m ([991/92]) as his second wife, BERNHARD [von Haldensleben], son of DIETRICH Markgraf über den Gau der Heveller [Nordmark] & his wife --- (-[1044/51]).  He was installed in 1009 as BERNHARD 
2 CONC Markgraf der Nordmark.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 16.           PREMISLAVA Vladimirovna (-[1015]).  Baumgarten names the wife of Duke László and gives her origin but only cites one secondary source in support[134].  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has
2 CONC  not yet been identified.   m ([1000]) LÁSZLÓ "Szár/the Bald" Prince of Hungary, Duke between March and Gran, son of MIHÁLY Prince of Hungary Duke between March and Gran & Adelajda [Adleta] of Poland (-1029).
2 CONT
2 CONT 17.           DOBRONEGA MARIA Vladimirovna (before 1012-1087).
2 CONT
2 CONT ...m (1043) KAZIMIERZ I KAROL "Odnowiciel/the Renewer" Prince of Poland, son of MIESZKO II Lambert King of Poland & his wife Richeza [Ezzonen] (25 Jul 1016-19 Mar 1058).
2 CONT
