1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malfrida
2 CONT
2 CONT Malfrida
2 CONT
2 CONT Malfrida (died 1000) was the probably Bohemian wife of grand prince of Kiev Vladimir I of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary Chronicle mentioned about a death of woman named Malfrida. Russian historian Vasily Tatishchev supposed that Malfrida was a Bohemian wife of Vladimir I of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other historian supposed that Malfida was indical to Malusha.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably children Bohemian wife of Vladimir I of Kiev probably had two sons with him:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1) Svyatoslav of Smolensk (d. 1015)
2 CONT *2) Mstislav of Chernigov (d. 1036) - probably his mother was Rogneda of Polotsk.
