2 CONC s son of Olga.  His birth date is estimated on the assumption that he was a young adult when the De administrando imperio was compiled, before the death of Emperor Konstantinos VII in 959.  According to the Primary Chronicle he "w
2 CONC as but a child" in 946.  At an early age, Sviatoslav´s father appears to have established him in the northern town of Gorodishche, which indicates a claim to overlordship of the northern Scandinavian settlements.  The place is cal
2 CONC led "Nemogardas" in the De administrando imperio, which could be a corruption of Novgorod.  He succeeded his father as SVIATOSLAV I Grand Prince of Kiev, under the regency of his mother.  Kiev was besieged by the Pechenegs in 962.
