1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judith_of_Swabia  ''(Summer 1054 – 14 March ca. 1105?)''
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.thepeerage.com/p11459.htm#i114581 ''(b. 1047, d. circa 1100)''
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/GERMANY,%20Kings.htm#JudithMariaM1SalomonHungaryM2WladyslawI
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         JUDITH [Maria/Sophia] ([1054]-14 Mar [1092/96]).  The Annales of Berthold record the betrothal in 1059 of "Andreas Pannoniæ rex…filio suo Salomoni adhuc puero" and "sororem eius [Heinrici regis] minorem Iuditham"[403]. 
2 CONC  The Annales Yburgenses refer to the wife of "Ungariam…[rex] Salemannum" as "regis Heinrici sororem" but do not name her[404].  The Gesta Hungarorum records that King András forced the marriage of "Salomoni regi" and "Henricus imp
2 CONC erator…Sophiam suam filiam", specifying that she had earlier been betrothed to "filio regis Franciæ"[405].  Having left Hungary for Germany after her husband was deposed in 1074, she was living in Regensburg when her husband attem
2 CONC pted to reclaim the Hungarian throne.  She refused to receive him when he returned in 1083.  Her second marriage is confirmed by the Chronicæ Polanorum which records that King Władysław married "sororem imperatoris tertii Henrici,
2 CONC  uxorem prius Salemonis Ungariæ regis"[406].  The Chronicon Polono-Silesiacum specifies her name "Iudite"[407].  The necrology of Weltenburg records the death "II Id Mar" of "Iudita de Polonia soror Heinrici imperatoris IV"[408]. 
2 CONC  The necrology of Regensburg St Emmeran records the death "II Id Mar" of "Iudita regina"[409].  The necrology of Speyer records the death "II Id Mar" of "Iudda regina imperatricis filia"[410].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[Betrothed''' ([1055/59]) to [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-I-king-of-France/6000000000157358561 PHILIPPE de France], son of HENRI I King of France & his second wife Anna Iaroslavna of Kiev (1052-château de Melun, Seine-et
2 CONC -Marne 30 Jul 1108, bur Abbaye Saint Benoît-sur-Loire).  The Gesta Hungarorum records that King András forced the marriage of "Salomoni regi" and "Henricus imperator…Sophiam suam filiam", specifying that she had earlier been betro
2 CONC thed to "filio regis Franciæ"[411].  This could only refer to the future Philippe I King of France as it is unlikely that the emperor's daughter would have been betrothed to his younger brother.  This betrothal is not corroborated
2 CONC  in the western European primary sources so far consulted.  He succeeded his father in 1060 as PHILIPPE I King of France.''']'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (betrothed 1059, early 1063) SALOMON King of Hungary, son of ANDRÁS I "the Catholic" King of Hungary & his second wife Anastasia Iaroslavna of Kiev (1052-killed in battle 1087).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1089]) as his second wife, WŁADYSŁAW I HERMAN Prince of Poland, son of KAZIMIERZ I KAROL "Odnowiciel/the Renewer" Prince of Poland & his wife Dobronega Maria Vladimirovna of Kiev ([1043]-4 Jun 1102).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -------
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Salian (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #114581, b. 1047, d. circa 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=11 Dec 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT      Judith Salian was born in 1047. (1) She was the daughter of Heinrich III, Holy Roman Emperor and Agnes de Poitou. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Wladislaw I Herman, Duke of Poland, son of Casimir I, Duke of Poland and Dobronega Maria of Kiev, circa 1089. (1) She died circa 1100. (1)
2 CONT
