1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ANNA SVYATOPOLKOVNA, PRINCESS OF KIEV & CHERNIGOV
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Svyatopolkovna was the daughter of Svyatopolk II / Grand Duke of Kiev (1050 - 1113) and his first wife, an unidentified / unnamed "Bohemian Princess".  Princess Anna was the second of their four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Wikipedia mini - biography ("Sviatopolk II of Kiev") erroneously identifies Anna Svyatopolkovna as the daughter of Duke Svyatopolk's second wife, Olena / Elene of the Cumans.  The mini - biography, however, correctly notes that 
2 CONC Princess Anna (died 1136) was married to "Sviatoslav Davydych of Chernihiv (Chernigov)" and that Sviatoslav Davydych "turned into a monk upon her death".
2 CONT
2 CONT Sviatoslav Davydych was the fifth and youngest son of Davyd Sviatoslavich / Prince of Smolensk and Chernigov (c. 1055 - 1123) and his wife, "Feodosia".  It would appear that David adopted the name Nikolai Svyatoslav Lutsk upon tak
2 CONC ing holy orders. 
