1 OCCU дочь половецкого хана Тугоркан, дъщеря на куманския хан Тугор, неизвестно имя, возможно дочь чешского князя Спытигнева II
1 TITL khatun
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} OLENA / ELENE TOGOROVNA, DUCHESS OF KIEV
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, in 1094 Sviatopolk married to a daughter of Tugor Khan of the Kypchaks (Cumans) -- Olena.  They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) Anna (died 1136), married to Sviatoslav Davydych from Chernihiv, who turned into a monk upon her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.) Maria, married Piotr Wlostowic, castellan of Wroclaw and Polish palatinate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.) Bryachislav (1104 - 1127), possibly dethroned Iaroslav as the Prince of Turov in  1118 and thence may have ruled as Prince of Turov from 1118 - 1123).  (Iaroslav / Yaroslav, Prince of Volynya would have been Bryachislav's olde
2 CONC r half - brother)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.) Izyaslav (died 1127), possibly the Prince of Turov in 1123.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source -- "Sviatopolk II of Kiev" / en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sviatopolk_II_of_Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary -- The accuracy of this Wikipedia mini - biography / genealogy is problematic.  Anna Svyatopolkovna was the second child and eldest daughter of Sviatopolk II and his first wife, the unidentified / unnamed "Bohemian Prin
2 CONC cess".  Verification of the lives of sons Bryachislav and Izyaslav from other sources is notable in its absence............In contrast, the marriage of Maria to Piotr Wlostowic is verified in a wide variety of sources, sufficient 
2 CONC to validate at least this portion of the Wikipedia mini - biography / genealogy.
