1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Rostislav Yaroslavich''' or Rostislav of Ryazan - the youngest son of Yaroslav Svyatoslavich, the Grand Duke of Ryazan. Prince of Ryazan from 1143 to 1145, a descendant of Rurik in the VIII generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rostislav Yaroslavich, after the death of his father in 1129, owned Ryazan together with his brother Svyatoslav. Svyatoslav reigned in Ryazan, and Rostislav in Pronsk. After the death of his elder brother Yuri in 1143 and the tran
2 CONC sfer of Svyatoslav from Ryazan to Murom, Rostislav took the Ryazan throne. And 2 years after the death of his middle brother Svyatoslav in 1145, he already occupied the throne of Murom, and in Ryazan he left his son Gleb as govern
2 CONC or, thereby violating the patrimonial rights of the nephews of the Svyatoslavichs.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the period 1146 - 1151, Rostislav was an ally of Izyaslav Mstislavich Volynsky, Vladimir and Izyaslav Davydovich Chernigov in the fight against Yuri Vladimirovich Rostov and Svyatoslav Olgovich Novgorod-Seversky. When Izyaslav 
2 CONC Mstislavich occupied Kyiv and opposed Svyatoslav Olgovich, Yuri Dolgoruky undertook a campaign to help Svyatoslav. Then Izyaslav asked Rostislav to raid the Suzdal volosts, and Yuri had to return from the road. Izyaslav managed to
2 CONC  expel Svyatoslav from Severshchina, but in the same 1146, the Suzdal princes Rostislav and Andrei Yuryevich laid siege to Ryazan.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a result, Rostislav Yaroslavich, together with his son Gleb, had to flee to the Polovtsy, the Ryazan reign was taken by Davyd Svyatoslavich (and very soon, after his death - Igor Svyatoslavich), Murom - Vladimir Svyatoslavich. 
2 CONC But already in 1148, Rostislav managed to return Ryazan, and in 1151, Murom. In 1152, having heard about the ruin of his Gorodok, Yuri Dolgoruky sent for help to the Ryazan princes; Rostislav came to his call with the regiments of
2 CONC  Murom and Ryazan. The campaign ended in an unsuccessful siege of Chernigov.
