1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Northern France:
2 CONT
2 CONT NORTHERN FRANCE
2 CONT VALOIS, VEXIN & VERMANDOIS
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 04 April 2025
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfravalver.htm
2 CONT B.      COMTES de VERMANDOIS 1080-1214 (CAPET)
2 CONT
2 CONT HUGUES de France, son of HENRI I King of France & his second wife Anna Iaroslavna of Kiev (1057-Tarsus 18 Oct 1102, bur Tarsus, Church of St Paul).   … He died from wounds received fighting the Turks near Tarsus in Asia Minor[304]
2 CONC .  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (after 1067) as her first husband, ADELAIS Ctss de Vermandois, de Valois et de Crépy, daughter and heiress of HERIBERT [VI] Comte de Vermandois & his wife Adelais de Valois ([1065]-28 Sep [1120/24]).  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris F
2 CONC usniacensis names "Adelaide comitissa Veromandensium" as wife of "Hugonem Magnum"[305].  Her husband left her as regent in Vermandois when he left on crusade.  She married secondly (1103) as his first wife, Renaud de Clermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Hugues & his wife had [nine] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  MATHILDE de Vermandois.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records the proposed marriage of "Robertus comes Mellentinus" and the daughter of "Hugonis Crispeiensis comes" which was prohibited by "Yvo [episcopus]" on grounds of consanguinity, the 
2 CONC mutual descent of the two parties from "Gauterus Albus de Albamarla" being set out in the chronicle although the name of the daughter is not given[1338].  It is not known to which daughter this refers, but it may be Mathilde.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis refers to (but does not name) the second of the daughters of "Hugonem Magnum [et] Adelaide comitissa Veromandensium" as wife of "Radulfo de Baugenci", parents of "Simonem eiusdem loci princip
2 CONC em"[1339].  "Domnus Radulfus de Balgentiaco" donated a wood to La Trinité de Vendôme, with a reserve for "uxor eius domna Mathildis", by charter dated 1105[1340].  
2 CONT
2 CONT She is named in the testament of "Simon Balgenciacensis dominus" dated to [1146/53] which names "Radulfi mei patris et Matildis mei matris"[1341].  
2 CONT
2 CONT The fact that Mathilde was the eldest daughter is confirmed by the De Genere Comitum Flandrensium, Notæ Parisienses which records "Agnes uxor domini Ingelranni de Cociaco" as daughter of "domina de Baugenciaco primogenita [comitis
2 CONC  Hugonis li Maines]"[1342].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1090) as his second wife, RAOUL Seigneur de Baugency, son of LANCELIN Seigneur de Baugency & his wife --- (-[1130])
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20FRANCE.htm#RaoulBaugencydied1130
2 CONT
2 CONT Raoul & his second wife had eight children: 
2 CONT * i)          HUGUES .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  [1104/08]. 
2 CONT * ii)         SIMON de Baugency (-27 Aug [1153/54]).  … A charter dated 1154 records the deathbed confession of "Symonem domnum Balgentiaci" that he had unjustly appropriated property of La Trinité de Vendôme and the settlement by
2 CONC  "Lancelinus frater eius"[759].  The testament of "Simon Balgenciacensis dominus" dated to [1146/53] names "Radulfi mei patris et Matildis mei matris" as well as "domine Adenordis", recording that the last named was then deceased 
2 CONC and implying but not stating explicitly that she was Simon's wife[760].  The testament makes no reference to any children.
2 CONT * iii)        LANCELIN [III] (-before 1192). 
2 CONT * iv)        RAOUL (-after May 1148).  “Mahildis mater Simonis de Baugencio” donated “terram...apud Venum” to the priory of Saint-Barthélemy de Semoy, with the consent of “filiis meis Simone, Lanscelino atque Radulfo”, by undated 
2 CONC charter[768]. 
2 CONT * v)         GUILLAUME .  before [1149].  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT * vi)        AGNES de Baugency .  The De Genere Comitum Flandrensium, Notæ Parisienses records "Agnes uxor domini Ingelranni de Cociaco" as daughter of "domina de Baugenciaco primogenita [comitis Hugonis li Maines]"[769].  A more 
2 CONC explicit reference which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  m (1132) ENGUERRAND [II] de Coucy, son of THOMAS Seigneur de Coucy & his third wife Mélisende de Crécy (-after 1147, bur Nazareth). 
2 CONT * vii)      MATHILDE de Baugency .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  [1104/08].  m EUDES [Archambaud] [III] Seigneur de Sully, son of GUILLAUME de Blois Seigneur de Sully &
2 CONC  his wife Agnes de Sully (-after 1162). 
2 CONT * viii)     [HERVE .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  [1140/43].  Abbé d'Ourscamp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Wikipedia page of her father, Hugh I Count of Vermandois:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_I,_Count_of_Vermandois
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda(1080-1130), married Ralph I of Beaugency
2 CONT
