1 NOTE Line 1740 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT   TITL [Count of Vermandois]
1 NOTE Married 3 times
2 CONT First, he was married in 1125 with Eléonore of Blois, daughter of Stephen II, Count of Blois. Their marriage ended in divorce in 1140. They had one son: 
2 CONT Hugh II "The Monk", count of Vermandois and Valois, resigned his titles in 1160 and became a monk, canonized 1177 (b. Amiens, 9.4.1127 - m. Caerfroy Cloister, near Paris, 4.11.1212).
2 CONT
2 CONT Second, he was married in 1140 with Petronilla of Aquitaine; in 1151 their marriage was dissolved. They had two children: 
2 CONT Elizabeth Mabile, countess of Vermandois and Valois (b. 1143 - d. Arras, 28 March 1183), married Philip I of Lorraine, count of Flanders. 
2 CONT Raoul II, count of Vermandois and Valois (b. 1145 - d. of leprosy, 1167). married Margaret of Lorraine, later countess of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT Third, he was married in 1152 with Laurette of Flanders, daughter of Thierry, Count of Flanders and Swanhilde. They had one daughter: 
2 CONT Eleonore, countess of Vermandois and Valois, renounced her titles in 1214 in favor of the French Crown and became a nun (b. 1152 - d. aft.1222). She married five times: 
2 CONT (probably) Godfrey of Hainaut, Count of Ostervant (d. 1163). 
2 CONT before 1167 Count William IV of Nevers. 
2 CONT ca 1170 Matthew of Lorraine, Count of Boulogne. 
2 CONT ca 1175 Count Mathieu III of Beaumont-sur-Oise. 
2 CONT ca 1210 Etienne II of Blois, Lord of Chatillon-sur-Loing 
1 NOTE Line 1740 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT   TITL [Count of Vermandois]
1 NOTE Raoul I of Vermandois (French: Raoul Ier "le Vaillant"; English, Ralph of Vermandois) (1085 - 14 October 1152), Count of Vermandois. He was son of Hugh of Vermandois and Adele of Vermandois.
2 CONT
2 CONT His paternal grandparents were Henry I of France and Anne of Kiev. His maternal grandparents were Herbert IV of Vermandois and Adele of Valois.
2 CONT
2 CONT His only paternal uncle was Philip I of France. Through him Raoul was a first cousin of Louis VI of France and a first cousin, once removed of Louis VII of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raoul served as the seneschal of France during the reign of his cousin Louis VII. Under pressure from Queen consort Eleanor of Aquitaine, Louis allowed him to repudiate his wife Eléonore of Blois in favor of Eleanor's sister, Pet
2 CONC ronilla of Aquitaine. This led to a war with Theobald II of Champagne, who was the brother of Raoul's first wife Eleonore. The war lasted two years (1142-44) and ended with the occupation of Champagne by the royal army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raoul and Petronilla were excommunicated by Pope Innocent II for their illegitimate marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT Raoul was married three times:
2 CONT
2 CONT First, he was married in 1125 with Eléonore of Blois, daughter of Stephen II, Count of Blois. Their marriage ended in divorce in 1140. They had one son: 
2 CONT Hugh II "The Monk", count of Vermandois and Valois, resigned his titles in 1160 and became a monk, canonized 1177 (b. Amiens, 9.4.1127 - m. Caerfroy Cloister, near Paris, 4.11.1212). 
2 CONT Second, he was married in 1140 with Petronilla of Aquitaine; in 1151 their marriage was dissolved. They had two children: 
2 CONT Elizabeth Mabile, countess of Vermandois and Valois (b. 1143 - d. Arras, 28 March 1183), married Philip I of Lorraine, count of Flanders. 
2 CONT Raoul II, count of Vermandois and Valois (b. 1145 - d. of leprosy, 1167). married Margaret of Lorraine, later countess of Flanders. 
2 CONT Third, he was married in 1152 with Laurette of Flanders, daughter of Thierry, Count of Flanders and Swanhilde. They had one daughter: 
2 CONT Eleonore, countess of Vermandois and Valois, renounced her titles in 1214 in favor of the French Crown and became a nun (b. 1152 - d. aft.1222). She married five times: 
2 CONT (probably) Godfrey of Hainaut, Count of Ostervant (d. 1163). 
2 CONT before 1167 Count William IV of Nevers. 
2 CONT ca 1170 Matthew of Alsace. 
2 CONT ca 1175 Count Mathieu III of Beaumont-sur-Oise. 
2 CONT ca 1210 Etienne II of Blois, Lord of Chatillon-sur-Loing 
