1 NAME Fleuri /de France/ seigneur de Nangis
2 GIVN Fleuri
2 SURN de France
2 NSFX seigneur de Nangis
2 _MARNM de France
2 NICK Flonrent
2 NICK Florus
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1095
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1119
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''FLEURI [Florus] de France''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm#PhilippeIdied1108
2 CONT
2 CONT ([1095]-after 1119)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Historia Regum Francorum Monasterii Sancti Dionysii names "Philippum et Florum et filiam unam" children of "Philippus rex [et] Fulconi Rechin Andagavorum comiti uxorem"[312].  His parentage is also recorded by Orderic Vitalis[
2 CONC 313].  A document dated Jul 1213 records that [314].  He was living in Anjou with his mother in 1117.  Seigneur de Nangis, by right of his wife.  m [--- de Nangis, daughter & heiress of --- de Nangis & his wife ---].  Her parentag
2 CONC e and marriage are assumed because her daughter is called "Isabellis de Nangies" in the source quoted below.   Fleuri & his wife had [two] children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT  a)  ISABELLE de Nangis
2 CONT
2 CONT  ([1118]-[after 1166/67]).  Documents dated Jul 1213 and Aug 1213, relating to the consanguinity between Erard de Brienne Seigneur de Ramerupt and his wife Philippa of Jerusalem, record "rex Franciæ…Grossus rex fratrem…Florium…fil
2 CONC ia Isabellis de Nangies…domina de Venisiaco", adding that her daughter was "domina de Venisiaco, mater…[Erardum de Rameruco] [Erardum de Brena]", another document in the series clarifying that Isabelle was the mother of "Aalaidis 
2 CONC dominæ Venisiaci…mater…Erardi"[315].  Dame de Nangis.  A charter dated to after 1151 recites the donation of “feodum de Thori” by “Symon Pichered” to Dilo abbey, confirmed by "Garnerus…de Venisiaco a quo feodum illud Symon tenebat
2 CONC  et uxor Garini Petronilla sed et filius eius Ansellus", and a later donation confirmed by "Ansellus…de Venisiaco…et frater Anselli, Freherus, sed et uxor sua Elisabeth", as well as other donations by Anseau, Isabelle and Ferry[31
2 CONC 6].  She is named in the cartulary of Preuilly[317].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln, Isabelle married firstly "Guy de Marolles", adding that he joined the crusade in 1141 and died in Palestine[318].  The primary source on w
2 CONC hich this is based is not known.  However, under a charter dated to [1166/67], Louis VII King of France confirmed donations of property to the abbey of Barbeau, including the donation of "apud capellam de Sarnai" made by "Guidonis
2 CONC  de Nangiis…cum assensu uxoris sue Helisabeth" and with the consent of "Milo de Corteriaco…uxore et filiis"[319].  It is possible that "Guidonis de Nangiis" is the same person as Guy de Marolles, and that his wife "Helisabeth" was
2 CONC  Isabelle de Nangis.  If this is correct, Guy would have been Isabelle´s second husband not her first, assuming that the charter relates to then current donations.  This would also be consistent with her supposed daughter by this 
2 CONC marriage having given birth to children from her second marriage (to Adam de Melun) in the 1180s.  Her descendants by this supposed second marriage were studied by Maurice Lecomte[320].  m [firstly] ([1136]) ANSEAU de Venizy, son 
2 CONC of GUERIN de Venizy & his wife Pétronille ---.  [m secondly GUY [de Marolles], son of --- (-after [1166/67]).  Seigneur de Nangis, de iure uxoris.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         [daughter .  Her parentage and marriage are recorded in Europäische Stammtafeln which also states that she was "Dame de Châtel-les-Nangis"[321].  The primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  H
2 CONC owever, as noted above under her supposed sister Isabelle, under a charter dated to [1166/67] Louis VII King of France confirmed donations of property to the abbey of Barbeau, including the donation of "apud capellam de Sarnai" ma
2 CONC de by "Guidonis de Nangiis…cum assensu uxoris sue Helisabeth" and with the consent of "Milo de Corteriaco…uxore et filiis"[322].  The consent given by "Milo de Corteriaco" and his wife and children would be consistent with he and 
2 CONC his wife also having an interest in the property donated, which would be the case if his wife was the sister of Isabelle de Nangis.  Her husband´s connection with the Melun family has not been confirmed.  m MILON [de Melun] Seigne
2 CONC ur de Courtry, son of ---.]  
