1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Sviatoslav_I
2 CONT
2 CONT of the Rurik Dynasty
2 CONT Sviatoslav or Svyatoslav I Igorevich (Old East Slavic: Свѧтославъ Игорєвичь, romanized: Svętoslavŭ Igorevičǐ; Old Norse: Sveinald; c. 943 – 972) was Prince of Kiev from 945 until his death in 972. He is known for his persistent ca
2 CONC mpaigns in the east and south, which precipitated the collapse of two great powers in Eastern Europe, Khazaria and the First Bulgarian Empire. He conquered numerous East Slavic tribes, defeated the Alans and attacked the Volga Bul
2 CONC gars, and at times was allied with the Pechenegs and Magyars (Hungarians).
2 CONT
2 CONT {The Khazar empire was overrun by Svyatoslav of Kiyev around the year 969}.
