2 CONT
2 CONT Russian academics Anna Litvina and Fjodor Uspenskij comment on the marriage of Vsevolodna and Khan Baszkord in 1152.  Litvina and Uspenskij note that "the position of princely widows in Rus' was rigidly ordained", with widows unab
2 CONC le to "plan on a second marriage in their homeland".  Litvina and Uspenskij note that this second marriage was not only advantageous to her son, Sviatoslav Vladimirovich / Prince of Vshchizh, but also her brother in law from her f
2 CONC irst marriage (Iziaslav III Davidovich / Grand Prince of Kiev).  Litvina and Uspenskij speculate that Princess Vsevolodna "fled to the Polovtsi with the connivance of the clan of her (first) Russian husband" and note that this was
2 CONC  "an entirely unheard of situation for Rus'".
2 CONT
2 CONT Source -- "Russo - Polovtsian Dynastic Contacts As Reflected In Genealogy And Onomastics"
2 CONT
2 CONT www.silkroad.com/newsletter/vol12/Litvina-SR12-2014-pp65-75.pdf
