2 CONT >Gianni II, called 'the Accursed' (Maledictus), was the son of Lamberto of Spoleto. He was the count of the palace of Salerno in 980 and acting regent for Pandolfo II of Salerno, a son of Pandolfo I 'the Iron-Head', principe di Ca
2 CONC pua e Benevento, duca di Spoleto. He was pushed out with Pandolfo II by Manso I, duke of Amalfi, in 981. The rule of Manso and his son Gianni I was oppressive and the local populace rose in revolt and elected the Spoletan Gianni I
2 CONC I prince in 983, expelling Manso. Gianni married '''Sigelgaita di Benevento''', daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Landolfo-II-IV-il-Rosso-principe-di-Capua-e-Benevento/6000000004533664301  Landolfo II], principe di Benevent
2 CONC o e Capua, and his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Yvantia/6000000184030870923 Wanzia], and sister of [https://www.geni.com/people/Pandolfo-I-principe-di-Benevento-Capua-e-Salerno/6000000000945074495 Pandolfo I 'the Iron-Head'].
2 CONC  Their son Guaimar III would have progeny. 
2 CONT
