2 CONT * 1.         GUIDO (-988).  The dating clause of a charter dated Jan 984, which records a donation by "Cicenus et Mari germani filii Adelghisi" and others, refers to the first year of "principatus domni nostri Iohanni et domni Gui
2 CONC doni eius filio…principibus"[917].  The Catalogus Principum Salerni record that "Wido eius filius [=Ioannes Maledictus]" ruled jointly with his father for 3 years 6 months before he died in a fire[918].  
2 CONT * 2.         GUAIMAR (-[Feb/Jun] 1027).  The dating clause of a charter dated Apr 989, which records a donation by "Lando…episcopus sanct sedis Pestane", refers to the sixth year of "principatus domni nostri Iohanni…principis" and
2 CONC  the first year of "principatus domni Guaimarii principis filio eius"[919].  He succeeded his father in 999 as GUAIMAR III Prince of Salerno.  -        see below.  
2 CONT * 3.         IOANNES (-[Nov 1031/Aug 1034]).  A charter dated Oct 989 names "domne Sichelgaita principissa uxor…domni Iohanni…principis" and "domnus Guaimarius princeps et Iohannes comes germani filii…domni Iohanni et domne Sichel
2 CONC gaite"[920].  m ---.  The name of Ioannes´s wife is not known.  Ioannes & his wife one child:  
