2 CONT a)         GEOFFROY de Medania (-after Mar 1116).  "Robbertus filius bone memorie Iordanis principis procurator…principatus Capuæ" donated property, at the request of "Goffridi de Medania", by charter dated Apr 1106[666].  Lord of
2 CONC  Acerra.  "Gaufridus qui vocor de Medania Suessolanorum et Acerranorum…senior" donated property, for the souls of "…Roberti barbani mei", by charter dated Mar 1116, subscribed by "Sikelgarda sua conjux…Robertus de Medania"[667].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SICHELGAITA, daughter of --- (-after Mar 1118).  "Gaufridus qui vocor de Medania Suessolanorum et Acerranorum…senior" donated property, for the souls of "…Roberti barbani mei", by charter dated Mar 1116, subscribed by "Sik
2 CONC elgarda sua conjux…Robertus de Medania"[668].  Stasser suggests that she was Sichelgaita di Salerno, daughter of Landolf di Salerno & his wife Emilia di Gaeta[669].  He argues convincingly that the only way of explaining why Enric
2 CONC o di San Severino, son of Roger di San Severino & his wife Sika di Salerno, names her son "Robertus de Medania uterinus frater"[670], is that the term "uterinus frater" must be interpreted in this document as maternal cousin.  
2 CONT
