2 CONT 2.         --de Courtenay (-after 1162).  William of Tyre records her parentage (but not her name), specifying that she was abbess at the convent of Maria Majoris near the Holy Sepulchre in Jerusalem and "iam natu grandævam" when 
2 CONC she testified about the consanguinity between Amaury I King of Jerusalem and his first wife (her niece) when their marriage was annulled in 1162[100]. 
