2 CONT a)         SERLON (-killed in battle near Nicosia, Sicily summer 1072).  Malaterra names "Serlonem nepotem suum [Rogerii]…Serlonis fratris suis filium" when recounting that he came to Italy, helped his uncle Roger in the capture o
2 CONC f Messina (in 1061), and in a later passage that he distinguished himself at Cerami (in 1063)[86].  It was intended that he should share in the government of Sicily[87], but he was killed in battle before this could be implemented
2 CONC .  Malaterra records that "nepotis sui Serlonis…" was killed "apud Siciliam a Saracenis"[88].  
2 CONT
