2 CONT - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#GodefroibrotherRobertMontescaglioso (half bro)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         GODEFROI .  The Gesta Roberti Wiscardi names "Robertus de Scabioso Monte comes…Gosfredi frater, et ambo orti germana fuerant ducis"[909].  Guerrieri highlights that "Gosfredi" in this passage has been identified as Gode
2 CONC froi Conte di Conversano but that it is not possible to confirm whether this is correct[910]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#GodefroiConversanodied1101
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GODEFROI [Geoffroy] (-[Sep] [Feb 1104/Apr 1107]). Malaterra names "Gaufridum de Conversano neptem suis [Roberti ducis]…filius…sororis suæ"[688].  The Gesta Roberti Wiscardi names "Robertus de Scabioso Monte comes…Gosfre
2 CONC di frater, et ambo orti germana fuerant ducis"[689].  Guerrieri highlights that "Gosfredi" in this passage has been identified as Godefroi Conte di Conversano but that it is not possible to confirm that this is correct[690].  If t
2 CONC he speculation is right, Godefroi was the same person as Godefroi, son of Armand Comte de Mortain & his wife Beatrix de Hauteville.  Conte di Conversano.  Lord of Nardò.  "Robertus comes Lorotelli, Amicus inclitus comes, Riccardus
2 CONC  Andrie comes, Goffredus comes Cupersani, Petrus comes de Lesena, Robertus comes filius Guillelmi Ybonis comitis" declared the restitution of property to the monastery of Banzi by charter dated Jun 1063[691].  [The Chronicon Breve
2 CONC  Normannicum records the death in Apr 1063 of "Gauffredus comes" and that "Goffridus filius eius" captured Taranto and "Castru Motule"[692].  "Gauffredus comes" in this source can probably be identified as Godefroi Conte di Lorite
2 CONC llo (see CENTRAL ITALY), who is not otherwise recorded as having a son named Godefroi.  It is possible therefore that the Chronicon Breve incorrectly records his parentage and that the reference to the younger Godefroi, as well as
2 CONC  the succeeding passages in the same source, relate to Godefroi Conte di Conversano.  The Chronicon Breve Normannicum records "Goffridus comes" captured "Castanetum" in 1064[693].  The Chronicon Breve Normannicum records that "Gof
2 CONC fridus comes" captured "Montem Pillosum" in Jun 1068, that "Hydrontum" was recaptured in Oct 1068, that "Goffridus comes" led a large fleet in attacking Brindisi in 1070, and captured Palermo in 1072[694].]  Protospatarius records
2 CONC  "magnum homicidium factum…in civitate Brundusii" in Jan 1070 and that "Robertus dux" entered Brindisi in 1071[695].  Presumably Godefroi was appointed Lord of Brindisi after its capture, but the date of his appointment has not be
2 CONC en confirmed in any of the primary sources so far consulted during the preparation of the present document.  According to Orderic Vitalis, he was nepos of Robert "Guiscard" Duke of Apulia who called him to his deathbed in 1085[696
2 CONC ].  "Goffridus…comes" donated land of S. Nicola to the abbot of Santa Maria di Nardò by charter dated May 1092, signed by "Sikelgaite comitisse, Roberti Cupersanensis…Rogerii vice comitis"[697].  "Goffridus…Brundusine civitatis do
2 CONC minator" donated property in the city of Brindisi to the abbess of Santa Maria veterana, in the presence of "Ursonis nostri vicecomitis", by charter dated Feb 1097[698].  "Goffridus…[co]me[s] dominator civitatis Neritoni…cum Seche
2 CONC lgayta comitissa uxore mea et cum filiis nostris [R]oberto et [A]lexandri[o]" donated the church of Santa Anastasia di Matino, near Gallipoli to the monastery of Santa Maria di Nardò by charter dated Jan 1099[699].  "Goffridus…com
2 CONC es, Brundusine civitatis dominator…et mea uxor domina Sichelgaita" donated the churches of the parishes of Santa Maria antica and San Andrea dell´isola, Brindisi to the church of San Leucio, Brindisi by charter dated Aug 1100[700]
2 CONC .  "Goffridus…comes dominator civitatis Neritoni…cum Sechelgayta comitissa uxore mea et cum filiis nostris domino Roberto et Alexandro" donated the church of SS Trinità, Nardò and other churches to the monastery of Santa Maria by 
2 CONC charter dated Feb 1104, signed by "Robertus infans, Alexander, Ugo vice come…"[701].  Lupus Protospatarius records the death in Sep 1101 of "Goffridus comes" and that "Alexius filius eius" invaded Materia, although the charter quo
2 CONC ted above, if correctly dated, shows that Godefroi was still alive in Feb 1104[702].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SICHELGAITA di Molise, daughter of RODULF de Moulins Conte di Boiano & his first wife Altruda di Guardia (-after Sep 1101).  "Goffridus…comes" donated land of S. Nicola to the abbot of Santa Maria di Nardò by charter dated
2 CONC  May 1092, signed by "Sikelgaite comitisse, Roberti Cupersanensis…Rogerii vice comitis"[703].  "Sikelgaita filia Rao de Mulisi" is named with "son époux Geoffroy de Conversano" in a charter dated Oct 1093[704].  "Goffridus…[co]me[
2 CONC s] dominator civitatis Neritoni…cum Sechelgayta comitissa uxore mea et cum filiis nostris [R]oberto et [A]lexandri[o]" donated the church of Santa Anastasia di Matino, near Gallipoli to the monastery of Santa Maria di Nardò by cha
2 CONC rter dated Jan 1099[705].  "Goffridus…comes, Brundusine civitatis dominator…et mea uxor domina Sichelgaita" donated the churches of the parishes of Santa Maria antica and San Andrea dell´isola, Brindisi to the church of San Leucio
2 CONC , Brindisi by charter dated Aug 1100[706].  "Goffridus…comes dominator civitatis Neritoni…cum Sechelgayta comitissa uxore mea et cum filiis nostris domino Roberto et Alexandro" donated the church of SS Trinità, Nardò and other chu
2 CONC rches to the monastery of Santa Maria by charter dated Feb 1104, signed by "Robertus infans, Alexander, Ugo vice come…"[707].  "Sichelgaita comitissa, Goffredi comitis…quondam uxor…meique filii domini Tanchedi…comes" donated "il c
2 CONC asale di Tuterano…il casale di Valerano, quello di Fenestrito" to the monastery of Santa Maria veterana di Brindisi by charter dated Apr 1107, signed by "Tanchredus comes---Constantia, Raimundi filius magni Raimundi…Sendi nepotis 
2 CONC comitisse…"[708].  "Rogerius…Sicilie et Italie rex…Rogerii primi comitis heres et filius" confirmed past donations by "…comitis quoque Goffridi Cupersani et uxoris eius Sikelgaite comitisse" by charter dated 28 Sep 1133[709].  God
2 CONC efroi & his wife had [eight] children: 
