2 CONT c)         ABELARD (-Constantinople after 1082).  The Gesta Roberti Wiscardi names (in order) "Gosfridus, Gocelinus, Abagelardus" as sons of "Unfredi"[217].  Guillaume of Jumièges records that “Umfridus” left “Abailardum filium su
2 CONC um” to the protection of “Roberto fratri suo...Wischardum cognominaverat” together with “ducatu Apuliæ”[218].  The Annals of Romoald record that "Bagelardum filium [=Onfridi]" was his father's successor in 1057 but was deprived an
2 CONC d expelled by his uncle Robert "Guiscard"[219].  His father appointed his uncle Robert Guiscard as his guardian 1057[220], but the latter seized his lands on the death of Onfroi.  Amatus recounts that "Abelard…his brother's son" w
2 CONC as among the conspirators against Robert "Guiscard"[221], undated but the context suggests this was in the early 1060s.  The revolt spread and was strengthened by a contingent of Varangians which arrived from Constantinople in 106
2 CONC 6, captured Bari, Brindisi and Taranto, but was recalled to Byzantium in 1068 to fight the Seljuks.  Abelard capitulated in early 1068.  The Cronica Trium Tabernarum et de civitate Catanzarii records that "Robertus Guiscardus" gra
2 CONC nted "Tabernam" to "Baialardo nepoti suo, Unfredi comitis filio" who rebelled against the duke and granted Taberna to "Guillelmo Capriolo cum nepte sua Adilitia"[222].  He was one of the leaders of the rebellion against Robert Gui
2 CONC scard in autumn 1078[223], seeking refuge in the Byzantine province of Illyria after the rebellion was crushed.  The Chronicon Breve Normannicum records that "Abiligardus comes" captured "Trojam", expelling "Boamundum filium Roger
2 CONC ti Ducis", and "Asculum" in 1079, although the latter was recaptured by Duke Robert after which "Abiligardus cum militibus suis" fled to Constantinople where he died[224].  Lupus Protospatarius names "Baialardus filius Umfredæ", w
2 CONC hen recording his capture of Ascoli in 1079[225].  "…Abbajelardus" was among the subscribers of the charter dated Jun 1080 under which "Rubbertus…dux et uxor mea Sykelgaita ducissa et filius meus Roggerius" made donations to Monte
2 CONC cassino[226].  Lupus Protospatarius records "Baialardus" leaving for Constantinople in 1082[227].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after 3 Feb 1079) --- [Argyre], daughter of [--- Argyros & his wife ---].  The Gesta Roberti Wiscardi records that "Argiricius" married his daughter to "Abagelardus, filius Unfredi"[228]. 
