2 CONC ke it worse, Ralph's 2nd wife was also an Emma. Emily Zack Tabuteau's 1992 paper "The Family of Moulins-la-Marche in the Eleventh Century," does a good job of explaining this. Unfortunately she doesn't match them up to their Norma
2 CONC n counterparts and family beyond Moulins-la-Marche.
