1 OCCU Cavaliere Normanno, 1°conte di Paternò e signore di Catania.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ugo_di_Jersey ( T r a n s l a t e d )
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of a noble family from Maine, he arrived in Sicily after having married Flandina d'Altavilla, daughter of the Grand Count Ruggero and Giuditta d'Evreux.  Following this marriage, Jersey '''had the county of Paternò as a
2 CONC  dowry'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1071 the Normans conquered the city of Catania, of which it assumed the lordship.  A few years later, with the departure of Ruggero towards Mileto, the people of Catania recalled the emir to the city, who then returned under th
2 CONC e Saracen rule [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1075 Ugo, together with his brother-in-law Giordano d'Altavilla, organized the siege of Catania with a contingent of 30 horses.  Benavert, the emir of Syracuse, made aware of the attack, received reinforcements from North Afric
2 CONC a and organized a surprise attack in a wood near the city of Etna against the Norman contingent stationed in the area.  It was an extermination that cost the lives of most of the Norman soldiers and of Jersey itself, which fought 
2 CONC to the last.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Flandrina he had a daughter, Maria de Paternione, who married Costantino d'Embrun - Paternò, son of Roberto d'Embrun, founder of the Paternò house, to whom he brought the county of Paternò as a dowry.  And from that moment th
2 CONC e descendants of Constantine therefore took the name of Paternò
