2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Robert [I] de Bassonville probably originated in the area of Caux, Normandy.  Three charters of the monastery of Saint-Victor-en-Caux refer to "Vassunvilla": Hugues Archbishop of Rouen confirmed donations to Saint-Victor-en-Caux
2 CONC , including property "in Vassunvilla" {Vassonville, commune du canton de Tôtes}, by charter dated 1137[1059].  "Hugo de Mortuo mari" confirmed the donations to Saint-Victor-en-Caux by "patre meo Radulfo…ab avo meo Rogerio", and ot
2 CONC her past donations, by undated charter, witnessed by "…Renaldum de Vassumvilla…"[1060].  "H. de Mortuomari" donated the church of Vatterville to Saint-Victor-en-Caux by charter dated to after 1179, witnessed by "…Reginaldo de Vass
2 CONC unvilla…"[1061]. ''
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NEAPOLITAN%20NOBILITY.htm#RobertBasunvilladied1142
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''ROBERT [I] de Bassonville''' [Basunvilla] "Chaperon" (-before Sep 1142).  Roger II King of Sicily invested him as Conte di Conversano in 1136. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1110) '''JUDITH of Sicily''', daughter of ROGER I Count of Sicily & his second wife Eremburge de Mortain (-before 19 Oct 1136).  "Jullita filia comitis Rogerii cum consensus fratris mei Rogerii regis Sicilie ducatus Apuli
2 CONC e et principatus Capue" founded a Cluniac abbey at Sciacca by charter, dated 1103 although this date appears incorrect in view of the title attributed to her brother which he only acquired in 1130[744].  The primary source which c
2 CONC onfirms her marriage has not yet been identified, although it is suggested by Ioannes Kinnamos who names "Bassavilla Rogerii Siciliæ tyranni ex sorore nepos"[745].  It also suggested by the Chronicle of Romualdo Guarna which recor
2 CONC ds that "Robertus de Basavilla comes de Conversano consobrinus frater eiusdem regis" was present at the coronation of Guillaume I King of Sicily (in 1154)[746].  "Robert de Bassonville comte de Conversano" donated the church of Sa
2 CONC n Martino di Molfetta to Cava by charter dated 19 Oct 1136 which names "feue Judith femme du comte et Robert leur fils"[747].  
2 CONT
2 CONT    Robert & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         ROBERT [II] de Basunvilla'(-15 Sep 1182).  William of Tyre names him and specifies that he was the son of the "amita" of Guillaume I King of Sicily[748].  "Robert de Bassonville comte de Conversano" donated the church 
2 CONC of San Martino di Molfetta to Cava by charter dated 19 Oct 1136 which names "feue Judith femme du comte et Robert leur fils"[749].  Ioannes Kinnamos names "Bassavilla Rogerii Siciliæ tyranni ex sorore nepos"[750].  He succeeded hi
2 CONC s father as Conte di Conversano.  "… ... ... ... ... ...  '''m''' as her second husband, ADELISA of Sicily, divorced wife of IOZZELINO Conte di Loreto, [illegitimate] daughter of ROGER II King of Sicily & his [mistress ---] (-afte
2 CONC r [1184/87]).  ... ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         GUILLAUME de Basunvilla .  Ioannes Kinnamos names "Gulielmus Bassavillæ frater"[769]. 
2 CONT
