2 CONT c)        ''' ['''--- di Molise .  The Ignoti Monachi Chronica records that in 1141 King Roger married "sororem comitis Ugonis de Molisio" by whom he had "filium Symonem, quem constituit principem Capue"[840].  Houben assumes that
2 CONC  she was the mistress of King Roger[841], but assuming the date quoted in the Ignoti Monachi Chronica is correct, it is not impossible that the couple married as it is after his first wife´s death and well before his marriage with
2 CONC  his known second wife.  
2 CONT
