2 CONT 14.       daughter .  Hugo Falcandus records that "Matthew [Bonellus] was captivated by the beauty of an illegitimate daughter of King Roger who had been married to Hugh Count of Molise"[550].  As this is probably dated to [1160/6
2 CONC 3] in this source, it is likely that she was one of the younger children of King Roger, born not later than [1130].  
