2 CONT 15.       ADELISA of Sicily (-after [1184/87]).  Chalandon states that Adelisa, daughter of King Roger II, married "Jocelin comte de Loreto"[551].  It is unlikely that Adelisa was the king´s daughter by his first marriage, as Romo
2 CONC ald only refers to one daughter whose death he records young.  The chronology suggests that she could not have been born from her father´s second or third marriages.  It is likely therefore that Adelisa was illegitimate.  Ctss di 
2 CONC Florenzia.  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (separated) JOSCELIN [Iozzelino] Conte di Loreto, son of RAMBOTUS Conte di Loreto & his wife --- (-1189).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ROBERT Conte di Loritello, son of ROBERT de Bassonville Conte di Conversano & his wife Judith of Sicily (-15 Sep 1182). 
