2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ## Father: Alfonso VII of León and Castile
2 CONT
2 CONT ## Mother: Berenguela of Barcelona
2 CONT
2 CONT ## Husband: Sancho VI of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT ## Sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Sancho VII, The Strong
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Fernando
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Ramiro or Remigio, bishop
2 CONT
2 CONT ## Daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Berenguela of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Blanca of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Constanza, died young
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancha_of_Castile,_Queen_of_Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha of Castile (c.1139-1179) was daughter of Alfonso VII of León and Castile and his first wife Berenguela of Barcelona. She was a member of the House of Burgundy-Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha was the fifth child of seven born to her parents, and sister of Sancho III of Castile, Ferdinand II of León, Constance, Queen of France, and half-sister of Sancha, Queen of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1157, Sancha married Sancho VI of Navarre. His reign was full of clashes with Castile and Aragon. He was a monastic founder and many architectural accomplishments date to his reign. He is also responsible for bringing his kingd
2 CONC om into the political orbit of Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho and Sancha had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho VII of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro, Bishop of Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengaria of Navarre (died 1230 or 1232), married Richard I of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca of Navarre, married Count Theobald III of Champagne, then acted as regent of Champagne, and finally as regent of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha died in 1179, aged forty and she left her husband a widower, he never remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancha_of_Castile,_Queen_of_Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho VI of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho VI of Navarre married Sancha of Castile in 1157, the daughter of Alfonso VII. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho VII of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro, Bishop of Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengaria of Navarre (died 1230 or 1232), married Richard I of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca of Navarre, married Count Theobald III of Champagne, then acted as regent of Champagne, and finally as regent of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha of Castile (c.1139-1179) was daughter of Alfonso VII of León and Castile and his first wife Berenguela of Barcelona . She was a member of the House of Burgundy-Spain .
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha was the fifth child of seven born to her parents, and sister of Sancho III of Castile , Ferdinand II of León , Constance, Queen of France , and half-sister of Sancha, Queen of Aragon .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1157, Sancha married Sancho VI of Navarre . His reign was full of clashes with Castile  and Aragon . He was a monastic founder and many architectural accomplishments date to his reign. He is also responsible for bringing his ki
2 CONC ngdom into the political orbit of Europe .
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho and Sancha had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho VII of Navarre  
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro, Bishop of Pamplona 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengaria of Navarre  (died 1230 or 1232), married Richard I of England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca of Navarre , married Count Theobald III of Champagne , then acted as regent of Champagne, and finally as regent of Navarre 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha died in 1179, aged forty and she left her husband a widower, he never remarried.
