2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Her ancestry is uncertain, although she was a member of the Taronites family. Europäische Stammtafeln II:177 says she was N.N. Taronitissa (Maria, as a nun), perhaps daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Michael-Taronites/60000
2 CONC 00025770926778 Michael Taronites]. Other sources say she was a daughter of Georgios Taronites Komnenos.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT  suggested daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Ioannes-Taronites/6000000009305101670 by:
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTINE%20NOBILITY.htm#TaronitissaMIoannesKomnenos
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       '''['''--- Taronitissa ([1125/30]-after 1176).  An anonymous poem records the marriage of Ioannes Komnenos and his wife "from the family of a pansebastos…the glory of the Taronites…on her paternal side issued from a bran
2 CONC ch of the same trunk…as she descends…from the race of the Komnenoi"[820].  According to Rüdt-Collenberg, she was the daughter or granddaughter either of Ioannes Taronites [I] or of his brother Gregorios (sons of Mikhael Taronites)
2 CONC [821].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[822], she was the possible daughter of Mikhael Taronites [II].  Jean Claude Chuat first proposed that she was the daughter of Ioannes Taronites [III][823].  This affiliation appears to 
2 CONC satisfy all the requirements of the text of the anonymous poem quoted above.  Her birth date range is estimated on the assumption that she was an adolescent or young adult at the time of her marriage.  She became a nun as MARIA af
2 CONC ter her husband died.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1146] ) IOANNES Doukas Komnenos protosébastos, son of ANDRONIKOS Komnenos sébastokrator & his wife Eirene [Aineiadissa] ([1128]-killed in battle Myriokephalon shortly after 17 Sep 1176).''']''' 
