2 DATE 1185
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Although a distinguished figure in the late Komnenian period, it is impossible to establish his family origin or his ties to the 11th-century Doukas dynasty. He is first attested in documents dating to 1166, where
2 CONC  he already bears the high court rank of pansebastos sebastos and is related to the ruling dynasty by marriage with a daughter of the sebastokrator Isaakies Komnenos and niece of Manuel I Komnenos, emperor of Byzantium. Their daug
2 CONC hter, possibly called Zoe, would have progeny, marrying the sebastokrator Ioannes Doukas Angelos. Makrodoukas next appears in 1170 and 1176, when he accompanied Emperor Manuel I in his campaigns against the Seljuk Turks. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Under Emperor Andronicus I Komnenos, Makrodoukas initially enjoyed the emperor's favour, and rose to the rank of panhypersebastos. However, after the rebellion of Makrodoukas' nephew Isaakios Dukas Komnenos, who declared himself 
2 CONC emperor on Cyprus, Makrodoukas was arrested along with other relatives of the rebel, accused of treason and condemned on 30 May 1185 to death by stoning. After surviving the stoning, he was dragged to Mangana, where he was dismemb
2 CONC ered."
2 CONT
2 CONT * Leo van de Pas,"[https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups=#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/70-ry7mhLS8 Constantine Doukas, 'Makrodoukas']", Feb. 22, 2013, at soc.genealogy.medieval.
2 CONT
