1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Michael Branas and Maria Komnene.  Maria Komnene was the great neice of Byzantine Emperor Alexios I Komnenos (1048 or 1056 - 1118).  Alexios Branas married Anna Komnene Vatatzaina, niece of Byzantine Emperor
2 CONC  Manuel I Komnenos (1118 - 1180).  Anna Komnene Vatatzaina was the youngest of seven children and only daughter of Theodoros Batatzes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source -- "Alexios Branas" / en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexis_Branas
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BYZANTIUM%2010571204.htm#AlexiosBranasdied1186
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''ALEXIOS Branas, son of --- (-1186).  Pansébastos, sébastos.'''  The record of the synod of 6 Mar 1166 records the presence of “...pansebasto sebasto domino Alexio Brana...”[935].  He led the army of Emperor Isaakios 
2 CONC II Angelos against the Normans, defeating them at Mosynopolis and Dimitritsa 7 Nov 1185, which resulted in their expulsion from Thessaloniki, Durazzo and Corfu[936].  He also led the Byzantine army against the Bulgarian rebellion 
2 CONC of the brothers Ivan Asen and Teodor in 1186, but having penetrated rebel territory he used the army for his own interests and led it to Adrianople where he was proclaimed Emperor ALEXIOS.  He marched on Constantinople, but was pu
2 CONC t to flight and killed[937].  m ANNA Komnene Batatzaina, daughter of ANDRONIKOS Komnenos Batatzes & his wife ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  Alexios Branas & his wif
2 CONC e had two children:
