2 CONT
2 CONT Einzelnachweise [Bearbeiten]
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ↑ Peter Csendes: Philipp von Schwaben. Ein Staufer im Kampf um die Macht, Primus-Verlag 2003, Seite 145,156,159,165
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. ↑ siehe Weblink: Irene Angelina in genealogie-mittelalter.de
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1193, Irene Angelina married Roger III of Sicily, but he died on 24 December 1193. Irene was captured in the German invasion of Sicily on 29 December 1194 and was married on 25 May 1197 to Philip of Swabia. In Germany, she was 
2 CONC renamed Maria.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was described by Walther von der Vogelweide as "the rose without a thorn, the dove without guile"
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, who had been deposed in 1195, urged her to get Philip's support for his reinstatement; her brother, Alexius, subsequently spent some time at Philip's court during the preparations for the Fourth Crusade. She thus had a
2 CONC n early influence on the eventual diversion of the Crusade to Constantinople in 1204.
2 CONT
2 CONT She bore four daughters with Philip, including our ancestor Marie of Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irene_Angelina for more information.
2 CONT
