2 CONT
2 CONT =Margaret of Hungary=
2 CONT
2 CONT ===! Not to be confused with Saint Margaret of Hungary. !===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret (Margit)''' (born 1175, living 1223) was the Empress consort of '''Isaac II Angelos''', Byzantine Emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT '''Margaret''' was the eldest daughter of '''Béla III of Hungary''' and his first wife '''Agnes of Antioch'''. She was a younger sister of '''Emeric of Hungar'''y. Her younger siblings were '''Andrew II of Hungary''' and '''Consta
2 CONC nce of Hungary'''. Two other siblings, '''Solomon''' and '''Stephen''', are mentioned in the "Europäische Stammtafeln: Stammtafeln zur Geschichte der Europäischen Staaten" (1878) by Detlev Schwennicke. They reportedly died young.[
2 CONC 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were '''Géza II of Hungary''' and '''Euphrosyne of Kiev'''.[2] Her maternal grandparents were '''Raynald of Châtillon''' and '''Constance of Antioch''' (joint princes of Antioch).[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==First Marriage==
2 CONT
2 CONT In Jan 1186, Margaret married the '''Byzantine Emperor Isaac II Angelos''', who wanted a politically strategic alliance with Hungary in order to strengthen his claim to the throne. Upon this marriage, Margaret took the baptismal n
2 CONC ame "'''Maria'''".
2 CONT
2 CONT *With Isaac, she had two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Manuel Angelos''' ( – d. 1212), he was evidently the elder son, being contemplated in 1205 to ascend the Byzantine throne[4]
2 CONT #'''John Angelos''' (b. ca. 1193 – d. 1259). He migrated to Hungary and ruled over Syrmia and Bacs (1227–42) as a vassal of king Béla IV of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac had been deposed and blinded in 1195 by his brother Alexios III Angelos who then assumed the throne. Isaac was imprisoned, but it's not yet clear if Margaret was also. Her step-son Alexios IV Angelos had escaped and went to 
2 CONC join the military discussions which were shortly to launch the Fourth Crusade. There, he and others convinced the Crusaders to attack Constantinople in order to depose this false uncle and restore his imprisoned father and himself
2 CONC  to the throne. This was done, but this restored reign was short-lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Second Marriage==
2 CONT Margaret's husband died in February, 1204, "whose end was accelerated by the fate of his son" "strangled in his dungeon after poison had failed to do its work".[5] When Boniface of Montferrat, commander of the land forces at the t
2 CONC aken of Constantinople, took the palace Vukoleon, it was found that Margaret had taken refuge there.[6] Boniface was one of only two contenders put forth to be elected the next Emperor, but he lost to Baldwin IX, Count of Flanders
2 CONC . As compensation, he was granted "all the territories on the Asiatic side of the Bosphorus as well as the Ille de Griesse [the Peloponnese]."[7] The coronation of the new Emperor took place in the church of St Sophia on 16 May 12
2 CONC 04. Later that year, in Constantinople the widowed Margaret, dowager Empress, married '''Boniface of Montferrat''', and returned to the rites of the Latin church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Boniface had just conquered that city in the Fourth Crusade, and was soon to become king of Thessalonica. Evidently in this same year of 1204, but after his new marriage, Boniface requested that he be allowed to exchange his lands
2 CONC  in Asia for the Kingdom of Thessalonica which he considered to be better suited for a political alignment with his new brother-in-law Andrew, then Regent of Hungary who would then be his neighbor, and the new Emperor agreed to th
2 CONC is exchange.[8] Boniface however did not enjoy his domains in peace, being engaged in almost constant warfare until his death. Margaret's step-daughter Agnes of Montferrat was married to the new Emperor Henry of Flanders in Feb 12
2 CONC 07. That same year, Boniface was returning to Thessalonica when attacked by a Bulgarian ambush. He was taken alive and decapitated, his head being sent to Kaloyan of Bulgaria.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT *With Boniface, Margaret had a son:
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Demetrius of Montferrat''' in 1207, he wed a sister of the Lord of Athens but they had no children Boniface left a will in which, he had designated Demetrius as his successor in Thessalonica, under the regency of his mother. H
2 CONC is son William, by an earlier marriage, succeeded to the Marquisate of Montferrat. The barons however, knowing that a strong government was necessary, constituted themselves a council of regency for the infant.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Third marriage==
2 CONT In 1207, on his father's death, Demetrius became king of Thessalonica, at least in title. The Emperor visited Thessalonica to receive the homage, in the infant's name but was barred from the city by the bailiff Biandrate until he 
2 CONC would agree to outrageous demands.[10] Margaret, now in the Emperor's presence, put herself in his hands and revealed the plot against the infant. At this time the Emperor crowned the new infant King of Thessalonica.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biandrate fled, but conspiring at a distance, returned once more in 1216 to claim the Regency. "In response to Queen Margaret's appeal the Emperor hurried to her assistance, but arrived on the scene only to die with mysterious sud
2 CONC denness in the flower of his age."[12] About 1216 Margaret fled to Hungary apparently leaving her son Demetrius in Thessalonica. 
2 CONT *She married thirdly '''Nicholas de St Omer''', who had accompanied his uncle on the Crusade and was granted a fief in Doris. He is also called "Lord of Boetia".[13][14] The Santameri hills in this area owe their name to a corrupt
2 CONC ion of "St Omer".[15]
2 CONT
2 CONT *With Nicholas, Margaret is apparently the mother of his two known sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT #'''Bela de St Omer''' (From Hungarian version: két fiúgyermek született, '''Béla''', 1208 után Saint-Omertban, meghalt 1240 után. - was born two sons, '''Bela''' born after 1208, in Saint-Omerta, died after 1240.) 
2 CONT #'''Guillaume de St Omer''', who married but died childless. (From Hungarian version: A második, '''Vilmos -Gulliaume''' született 1210 körül Flandriában, 1230 után elvette '''Margareta de Wavrin'''t, meghalt 1242. április 20-24 k
2 CONC özött Trauban. - The second, '''William - Gulliaume''' was born around 1210 in Flandria, after 1230 he married with '''Margareta de Wavrin''', died  20-24 April  1242 in Traun.)
2 CONT *Margaret was still living in 1223. Her exact death date and place, and burial location are apparently unknown.
