2 CONT Melissenos (Greek: Μελισσηνός), latinized Melissenus, '''feminine form Melissene (Μελισσηνή), latinized Melissena''', was the name of a noble Byzantine family that flourished from the late 8th century on until the end of the Byzan
2 CONC tine Empire and beyond.  ...
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 13th century, a branch of the family are attested as landowners around Smyrna,[3] while other branches of the family settled in the Morea and in Epirus, '''and a lady of the house even married Michael I Komnenos Doukas''', 
2 CONC the founder of the Despotate of Epirus.[15]
