2 CONT 1.         MARIJA (before 1221-after 1237).  Georgius Akropolites records that "rege Ioanne Asane…filia Maria ex pellice" married "Theodorus Comnenus…fratri suo Manueli"[314].  Ephræmius records the marriage of "Asane Ioanne…Maria
2 CONC m…notham filiam" and "Manueli"[315].  It is not known whether her alleged illegitimacy resulted from her mother's repudiation (as noted above) or whether her mother was the concubine not the wife of her father.  Her marriage was a
2 CONC rranged as part of the alliance with the Bulgarians agreed by her future husband's brother Emperor Theodoros[316].  Georgius Akropolites records that "fratrem Manuelem" sent back "coniugem ad Asanam patrem", dated from the context
2 CONC  to after her father's third marriage[317].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1225], repudiated [1238]) as his second wife, MANUEL Angelos Dukas Komnenos [Epirus], despot, son of IOANNES KONSTANTINOS Dukas Angelos, sebastokrator & his wife --- (-[1241]). 
2 CONT ------
