2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John III Ducas Vatatzes (1193-1254), Byzantine emperor (1222-1254), who, by his military successes and external policies, isolated the Latin Empire (see Byzantine Empire) and laid the groundwork for the reconquest of Constantinopl
2 CONC e (present-day İstanbul). Chosen to succeed his father-in-law, Theodore I Lascaris, John initially ruled only the area of Nicaea in Asia Minor, the remnant of the Byzantine Empire left him, but he expanded his realm by recovering 
2 CONC the Latin conquests in Anatolia and winning new territories in Bulgaria and Epirus. A strong administrator, John did much to improve the social, cultural, and economic conditions of his subjects.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NIKAIA.htm#IoannesIIINikaiadied1254B
