1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belek_Ghazi '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Belek Ghazi''' (''Nuruddevle Belek'' or ''Balak'') was a Turkish bey in the early 12th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Early life=
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was Behram and his grand father was Artuk, an important figure of the Seljuk Empire in the 11th century. He was a short-term governor of Suruç (now a district center in Şanlıurfa Province of Turkey). During the First Cr
2 CONC usade, the crusaders captured the city in 1098. He took part in the Seljuk expedition to Antakya which was recently lost to Crusaders. But the campaign ended in failure.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Beylik in Harput=
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1112 Belek captured Harput (an ancient city near to present day Elazığ in Turkey) from Mengüceks. He founded a beylik.[1] This beylik is now known as the Harput branch of the Artukids (the other two being the Hasankeyf branch o
2 CONC f Sökmen and Mardin branch of Ilghazi). Next year he married to Ayşe Hatun, widow of the late Anatolian Seljuk sultan Kılıç Arslan I . By this prestigious marriage, he formed family ties with the Seljuk family.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1120, Belek together with Danishmends defeated a coalition of Mengüceks and Constantine Gabras of the Byzantine Empire.[3] Two years later, after the death of Ilghazi, Belek became the leader of the Artukids.[4] In 1122 he defe
2 CONC ated the forces of Countship of Edessa and took Joscelin I as captive. Next year Baldwin II of Jerusalem too was enslaved by Belek. These two victories gained Belek fame both in Muslim countries and in Europe.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Death and aftermath=
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1124 he was invited to defend Tyre the only port the Muslims used in Syria against the attacking Crusaders. During the fighting he was killed on 6 May 1124.[2] Shortly after his death Harput was annexed by the Artukids of Hasan
2 CONC keyf. Nevertheless in 1185 another beylik was founded by Artukids in Harput.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT # Yücel-Yaşar, p.167
2 CONT # Belek Gazi
2 CONT # Yücel-Yaşar,p.153
2 CONT # Yücel Yaşar, p168
2 CONT
