1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sallar_of_Shirvan
2 CONT
2 CONT Sallar was the fifteenth Shah of Shirvan. He was the uncle and successor of Ali III (he deposed Ali III). Sallar was married to an unnamed daughter of Abu-l-Aswar Shavur I bin al-Fadl I. Sallar was one of youngest sons of Yazid II
2 CONC . In 1049, Sallar rebelled against his nephew Ali III; he repelled him from Shamakhi, and thereafter had him captured and killed near Baylaqan. In 1053, Sallar captured the Malu castle from pagans and then had it rebuilt.
2 CONT
2 CONT He later died on 20 February 1063, and was succeeded by his son  Fariburz I.
