2 CONT =Leo I, Prince of Armenia=
2 CONT Leo I[1](Armenian: Լեիոն Ա), also Levon I[2][3] or Leon I,[4] (unknown[2] – Constantinople, February 14, 1140[2]) was the fifth lord of Armenian Cilicia[3] or “Lord of the Mountains”[2] (1129[2][3]/1130[1]-1137[1][3]).
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children# (1100–1103) The name and the origin of his wife are not known with certainty.[2] It is possible that his wife was a daughter of Count Hugh I of Rethel, or she may have been the daughter of Gabriel of Meliten
2 CONC e.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT #(?) unnamed daughter, who was the wife of a “Frankish knight from Antioch”, and mother of the Regent Thomas[2]
2 CONT #unnamed daughter, the wife of Vasil Dgha[2]
2 CONT #(?)[2] Constantine[1] (? – Edessa, 1138/1144)[2]
2 CONT #Thoros II of Cilicia (? – February 6, 1169)[2]
2 CONT #Stephen (before 1110 – February 7, 1165)[2]
2 CONT #Mleh I of Cilicia (before 1120 – Sis, May 15, 1175)[2]
2 CONT #Roupen (after 1120 – Constantinople, 1141)[2] (Leo’s second marriage proposed by Rüdt-Collenberg is speculative.)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
