2 CONT *a)         [THOMAS (-murdered 1169).  William of Tyre records Thomas as "ex sorore [Melieris] nepos"[419].  As noted above, it is unlikely that this is correct assuming that his daughter married Thoros II (see below), a great-unc
2 CONC le/great-niece marriage being improbable.  Thomas was regent for Rupen II Lord of the Mountains in 1168.  The Chronicle of Sempad records that "the bailly Thomas" fled to Antioch after the murder of Stepane[420].  The Lignages d'O
2 CONC utremer record that "le baile Thomas" fled to Antioch when Mleh invaded Cilicia[421].] <br/> '''m''' ---.  The name of Thomas's wife is not known.  Thomas & his wife had one child: 
