1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Wikipedia:==
2 CONT '''A magyar nyelvű cikkből'''
2 CONT *[http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vazul '''Vazul'''] Ellenőrizve: 2013. szeptember 17.
2 CONT **Élt: 970 körül–1037
2 CONT **Apa: Mihály, Taksony fejedelem fia
2 CONT **Anya: bizonytalan-vitatott
2 CONT #bolgár hercegnő ((Mihályról szóló angol cikk szerint a Komitopuli-ház tagja (vitatott) /member of the Cometopuli dynasty/ (debated)), vagy kún, vagy kazár-kabar, esetleg volgai bolgár származású
2 CONT #Adelaide da Polónia (a Mihályról szóló portugál Wikipedia cikk szerint, amit az EuWeb „Arpad family” leszármazási összeállítás is tartalmaz. . A Geni-ben Vazul anyjaként  '''Adelajda - Adelheid Piastowna''' szerepel.
2 CONT **Feleség(ek): Tátony nemzetségbeli nő 
2 CONT
2 CONT **Gyermekek:
2 CONT #Levente
2 CONT #András
2 CONT #Béla
2 CONT *Testvér:  Szár László
2 CONT *Egyéb neves rokoni kapcsolat: I. István unokatestvére
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://bg.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%B0%D0%B7%D1%83%D0%BB '''Вазул''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''translated by Google Translator:''' Vazul is the grandson of Hungarian prince Taksony <sic)  Lasonc> and son of Michael. Vazul repeatedly involved in conspiracies against the first Hungarian Christian King István I, Vazul was e
2 CONC xcluded from the line of descendants of the Hungarian royal throne because he was pagan. However Arpad dynasty survived precisely through the sons of Vazul. Vazul has two marriages both in Bulgarian princesses:
2 CONT *Katun Anastasia, daughter of Tsar Samuil
2 CONT *Catalina granddaughter of Tsar Ivan Vladislav From his first marriage he had three sons – (from them) two Hungarian kings
2 CONT # Andrew I and
2 CONT # Bela I and their brother
2 CONT # Levente.
2 CONT -------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vazul (Basil) (11th century – died 1037) was a Hungarian noble of the Árpád family, Duke between Morava (March) and Esztergom (Hran or Gran). He was the grandson of Taksony. His father Michael (Mihály), Duke between Morava (March)
2 CONC  and Esztergom (Hron or Gran) (– ca 978 or bef. 997) and his mother was Michael's wife Adelajda of Poland (– aft. 997), daughter or sister of Mieszko I of Poland. His brother was Ladislaus the Bald. He was a cousin of Stephen I of
2 CONC  Hungary. He took part in a conspiracy aimed at the murder of king Stephen, since he was excluded from the royal succession in favour of Pietro Orseolo. The assassination attempt failed. Vazul had his eyes gouged out and molten le
2 CONC ad poured in his ears; his sons were exiled.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Vazul's three sons (with his wife from Tátony family or a woman who may (or may not) have been daughter of Tsar Samuel of the Bulgarians, Katun Anastazya) András (Andrew I), Béla and Levente, two would ascend the throne after t
2 CONC he dynastic struggle following the death of Stephen I. The line of Árpád kings following Stephen is therefore referred to as the Vazul line.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Wives
2 CONT
2 CONT Katun Anastazya
2 CONT
2 CONT Katalin
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vazul"
2 CONT
