2 CONT *1.         TAVEL ... m ---.  The name of Tavel's wife is not known.  Tavel & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT **a)         TORMAS [Termacs] (-killed in battle Augsburg Aug 955).  The De Administrando Imperio of Konstantinos Porphyrogenetos names "Termatzum" as the son of "Tebele"[228].  He stayed at the court of Emperor Konstantinos VII. 
2 CONC  Patriarch in Byzantium 948.  He was killed in battle against Otto I King of Germany at Augsburg.  m ---.  The name of Tormas's wife is not known.  Tormas & his wife had [two] children:  
2 CONT ***i)          KOPPANY (-killed in battle 998).  Duke in Sanyoy, in south-western Hungary.  He claimed the throne on the death of Prince Géza as most senior representative of the family, but was defeated and killed by István Princ
2 CONC e of Hungary.  The Gesta Hungarorum records that "duce Cappan" was killed after the coronation of "rex Stephanus" but gives no background to his death or indication of any family relationship with the king[229].  
2 CONT ***ii)         ['''daughter'''.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   She was known as '''PREDSLAVA in Russia'''.  Europäische Stammtafeln[230] suggests that '''Predslava was 
2 CONC the possible daughter of Tormas''' but the basis for this speculation is not known.  Her marriage date is estimated from the estimated date of birth of her son.  m (before [960]) SVIATOSLAV I Grand Prince of Kiev, son of IGOR [Ing
2 CONC var] of Kiev & his wife Olga ([941]-killed in battle 972).]  
2 CONT **b)         [ZERIND.]  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   
2 CONT **c)         [daughter.  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[231], she was the daughter either of Tavel or of Tavel's first cousin Tas.  The primary source on which this information is based has not yet been identified.  m LEL (-
2 CONC killed in battle Aug 955).] 
