2 CONT Prince of Kiev (912-)
1 NOTE Konge fra 912-945. Ukjent mor.
1 NOTE Dräpt 945 av drevljaner under ett skatteindrivingståg.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-2438
1 NOTE Igor, Grand Prince of Kiev
2 CONT Born circa 875 at Novogorod, Kiev
2 CONT Acceded: 924
2 CONT Died in 945, murdered by the Drevlanes from the town of Korosten
2 CONT   Although said to be less capable than leaders before and after him,Igor nontheless carried the conquests of Kievian Rus further. Heundertook campaigns against Persia, Constantinople and Bulgaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Igor married in 903 to St. Olga, Regent of Kiev, who was born circa 890and died in 969.Ancestral File Number:<AFN> B6DN-ZQ
1 NOTE OR "IGOR""INGVARR"; GRAND PRINCE OF KIEV 912-945; MURDERED
1 NOTE Line 5273 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT   NAME Igor Grand Duke Of /KIEV/
1 NOTE he conquered and established Kiev as the capital of the Varangian Empire. He ruled from 912 to 945. He was killed in battle against raiding slavers.
1 NOTE he conquered and established Kiev as the capital of the Varangian Empire. He ruled from 912 to 945. He was killed in battle against raiding slavers.
1 NOTE 1   Sources: RC 143; Clarkson; Riasanovsky; A. Roots 241; Kraentzler 1484. Grand Prince of Novgorod and Kiev. He was killed while collecting tribute in 945. He ruled from 913-945. His wife, St. Olga, acted as regent from 945-962. 
