1 OCCU Governor of Novgorod, воевода Владимира I Святославича, воевода
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Russia Rurikid:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Dobrinya is the brother of Malusha (Malfred), and son of Malk of Lyubech (d. 1002)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Russian Wikipedia page on Dobrynya (Governor):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D1%8B%D0%BD%D1%8F_(%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0)
2 CONT
2 CONT In English:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dobrynya was governor for Vladimir Svyatoslavich, and the brother of his mother Malusha. According to some sources, he is the son of Malk Lyubechanin or Msishi-Lyut (Mstislav) Sveneldich. He is the likely prototype for the hero Do
2 CONC brynya Nikitich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT When in 970 Grand Prince Svyatoslav divided Kiev rus between his two elder sons, the ambassadors of Novgorod, on instructions from Dobrynya, begged to be given Vladimir, who went to Novgorod with his uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Going in 979 from Novgorod to Kiev with the intent to wrest power from his elder brother, Vladimir wanted to rob Yaropolk of his bride, Rogneda, daughter of the Prince of Polotsk Rogvolod. Dobrynya accompanied. When Rogneda said "
2 CONC I do not want a robichich," it greatly offended Dobrynya's sister, whom they called a slave. After defeating Rogvolod, Dobrynya is documented as ordering his nephew to be "with her (Rogneda) in front of her mother and father."
2 CONT
2 CONT Having become the sole power, Vladimir assigned Dobrynya as Posadnik in Novgorod, which following the example of his nephew, placed on the Peryni coast of Volkhov, Perun. So in 985, he went with Vladimir to the rich Volga-Bolgars.
2 CONC  Peace with the Bolgars was concluded on the advice of Dobrynya, who said that such a rich nation that could afford to wear boots would not pay tribute and advised him to search for the Devil's clodhoppers.
2 CONT
2 CONT With regard to participation in the baptism, Dobrynya of Novgorod, it seems was recognized as trustworthy, but the news of the chronicles is uncertain and confused, and details of the episode have been taken by Tatischev from the 
2 CONC words of the so-called Ioakimovskoy Chronicle. This was the basis of the old Novgorod saying that Putyata baptized by the sword, and Dobrynya by fire."
2 CONT
2 CONT Some time later, Novgorod's mayor was the son of Dobrynya, Constantine Dobrynich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Prozorovsky and Shakhmatov (information about these ancestors are given by the authors of the Primary Chronicle Vyshata and Jan Vyshatich):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Malke Lyubchanin
2 CONT
2 CONT 1a. Malusha
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b. Dobrynya
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b1 Constantine Dobrynich
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b1a Ostromir and Theophanes
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b1a1 Vyshata
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b1a1a Putyata Vyshatich
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b1a1b Jan Vyshatich and Mary
2 CONT
2 CONT 1b1a1b1. Barlaam
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Dobrynya was Vladimir the Great's maternal uncle and tutor who was later transformed in Russian folklore into the invincible bogatyr Dobrynya Nikitich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dobrynya's life and extent of his influence on Vladimir are shrouded in speculation and controversy. It is fairly certain that his sister Malusha was Vladimir's mother. It is also generally accepted that Dobrynya's posadnik dynast
2 CONC y in Novgorod was continued by his son Konstantin Dobrynich and grandson Ostromir.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Novgorod chronicles, it was at his urging that Svyatoslav I sent his illegitimate son, Vladimir, to govern Novgorod, with Dobrynya as his tutor. Nine years later, Dobrynya persuaded Vladimir to wrest Kiev from his
2 CONC  brother Yaropolk. On their way to Kiev, Yaropolk's bride, Rogneda of Polotsk, offended Dobrynya by calling his sister a "bondswoman". Dobrynya took his revenge by arranging Rogneda's rape by Vladimir.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Vladimir's enthronment in Kiev, Dobrynya returned to rule Novgorod in his name. He accompanied his nephew in the 985 expedition against Volga Bulgaria and, following his lead, erected an idol of Perun on the bank of the Volk
2 CONC hov River. After the Baptism of Kiev, he is said to have forced the Novgorodians into Christianity "by fire".
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Wikipedia: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dobrynya English]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dobrynya (Russian: Добрыня) was Vladimir the Great's maternal uncle and tutor who was later transformed into the invincible bogatyr Dobrynya Nikitich in the Russian folklore.
