1 OCCU King of Norway, Norges konge/kung 1015-1028, King of Norway 1015-1028, Roi, de Norvège, , King of Norway, Gift 1019, Konge av Norge, Kung av Norge 1015-1028, Norges konge fra 1015 til 1028
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On July 29, 1030, King Olav Haraldsson was killed at the Battle of Stiklestad, north of Trondheim, cut down by his own countrymen. He was around 35. A Viking raider in his youth, he became king in 1015, worked to b
2 CONC ring Norway from paganism to Christianity, was driven into exile by Cnut the Great, and died trying to take his kingdom back.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the accounts, a light was seen over his body and a spring rose at his grave. When it was opened a year later his body was found incorrupt, and he was proclaimed a saint at Nidaros in 1031. Rome confirmed it in 1164. N
2 CONC idaros Cathedral was raised directly over his burial place and became one of the great pilgrimage destinations of Christendom.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was given a title no other Norwegian has held: Rex Perpetuus Norvegiae, the Eternal King of Norway. Every king since is understood to hold the crown only on loan from him.
2 CONT
2 CONT July 29 of each year is Olsok, his feast day, kept by both the Catholic and the Orthodox Church. The lion on Norway's coat of arms still holds Saint Olav's axe.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Olav II Haraldsson «the Saint/Digre» den Hellige==
