1 CONT Yaroslav I the Wise (c. 978, Kiev -20 February 1054, Kiev) (East Slavic: ??????? ?????? ; Christian name: George; Old Norse: Jarizleifr) was thrice Grand Prince of Novgorod and Kiev, uniting the two principalities for a time under
1 CONC  his rule. During his lengthy reign, Kievan Rus' reached a zenith of its cultural flowering and military power.
1 CONT
