1 CONT trusted in N. de Baumgarten's scholarship and professionalism---anddid not
1 CONT really check out the facts themselves. The Editor of a journal, suchas
1 CONT TAG, certainly cannot check out every fact and document himself. But,in
1 CONT this particular case, Jacobus gives the N. de Baumgarten material his
1 CONT personal imprimatur, as cited above [TAG 9:13, Paragraph 2]
1 CONT
1 CONT         So----has N. de Baumgarten in his "OrientaliaChristiana"---dealing
1 CONT with "The House of Rurik"---been totally discredited by subsequentrigorous
1 CONT scholarship---or does his judgment still seem credible to some serious
1 CONT scholars----or are there alternate explanations?
1 CONT
1 CONT         This is an intriguing question of interest to many folks whoare
1 CONT descended from Anne of Kiev (c. 1024-c.1066) [Anna Yaroslavna] whomarried
1 CONT Henry I, King of France.
