0 @N6000000002187805519@ NOTE Sviatoslav II of Kiev
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Sviatoslav Yaroslavich (1027 – December 27, 1076) was the Prince (Kniaz) of Chernigov from 1054 to 1073 and Grand Prince (Velikiy Knyaz) of Kiev from 1073 until his death. A son of Yaroslav I the Wise, he was a founder of Chernigo
1 CONC v princely line and is sometimes referred to as Sviatoslav of Chernigov.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT A page from Svyatoslav's MiscellaniesUpon his father's death in 1054, Sviatoslav joined his brothers Vsevolod and Iziaslav in forming a kind of a princely triumvirate that oversaw the affairs of Kievan Rus' until 1072. In 1067, th
1 CONC ey defeated their cousin, Vseslav of Polotsk, on the Nemiga river and took him prisoner. A year later, the brothers were smashed by the Polovtsi on the Alta River. After a while, Sviatoslav returned to defeat these steppe nomads w
1 CONC ith a small force at the town of Snov, thus enhancing his prestige among the populace. A part of the first Russian legal code Russkaya Pravda is assigned to the brothers.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sviatoslav's first wife was named Kilikia, a lady of unknown origin, but possibly a princess from the Caucasus. Their sons were Oleg, Gleb, Roman, and David. In 1072 Sviatoslav married Oda, daughter of a certain "Count Lippold", a
1 CONC nd the sister of Burkhard, provost of Trier. Oda's grand-uncles were Pope Leo IX and Henry III, Holy Roman Emperor.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1073, the triumvirate broke up, when Sviatoslav, supported by his younger brother Vsevolod, dethroned and replaced his older brother Iziaslav on the Kievan throne. Three years later, Russian scribes compiled the so-called Izbor
1 CONC nik Sviatoslava at his request. One of the oldest relics of the Old East Slavic language, the book is a compilation of articles on grammar, logic, poetics, church, sermons, riddles, and parables. One of the miniatures represents S
1 CONC viatoslav himself, standing with his second wife Oda and a son.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sviatoslav's son Oleg of Chernigov had a posterity which continues in male line to the present day. His son by Oda, Yaroslav, founded the great dynasty of Riazan, and the Seljuk Sultan Kilij Arslan II claimed to descend from one o
1 CONC f Sviatoslav's daughters.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Iziaslav I Prince of Kiev and Chernigov
1 CONT
1 CONT 1054–1076 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Vsevolod I 
0 @N6000000004533604516@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Svyatoslav Yaroslavich (1027—1076) was the Prince of Chernigov from1054 to 1073 and Grand Prince of Kiev from 1073 until his death. Hewas the son of Yaroslav I the Wise and father of Oleg Svyatoslavich.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT A page from Svyatoslav's MiscellaniesUpon his father's death in 1054,Svyatoslav joined his brothers Vsevolod and Iziaslav in forming a kindof a princely triumvirate that oversaw the affairs of Kievan Rus'until 1072. In 1067, they 
1 CONC defeated their cousin, Vseslav of Polotsk,on the Nemiga river and took him prisoner. A year later, the brotherswere smashed by the Polovtsi on the Alta river. After a while,Svyatoslav returned to defeat the steppe people with a sm
1 CONC all force atthe town of Snov, thus enhancing his prestige among the populace. Apart of the first Russian legal code Russkaya Pravda is assigned tothe brothers.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1073, the triumvirate broke up, when Svyatoslav, supported by hisyounger brother Vsevolod, dethroned and replaced his older brotherIziaslav on the Kievan throne. Three years later, Russian scribescompiled the so-called Izbornik
1 CONC  Svyatoslava at his request. One of theoldest relics of the Old East Slavic language, the book is acompilation of articles on grammar, logic, poetics, church, sermons,riddles, and parables. One of the miniatures represents Svyatos
1 CONC lavhimself, standing with his second wife Oda and a son. There is still acontroversy as to Oda's parentage, but it is known that her uncleswere Emperor Henry III and Pope Leo IX.
1 CONT
1 CONT Svyatoslav's son Oleg of Chernigov had a posterity which continues inmale line to the present day. A younger son by Oda founded the greatdynasty of Ryazan, and the Seljuk Sultan Kilij Arslan II claimed todescend from one of Svyato
1 CONC slav's daughters.
0 @N6000000000945084123@ NOTE Yelisaveta [Ellisiv, Elizabeth] og Harald hadde døtrene: 
1 CONT Maria, død 1066, og
1 CONT Ingegjerd.
1 CONT Fra Snorre Sturlasson: Harald Hardrådes saga:
1 CONT 83. Da kong Harald var ferdig, og han fikk bør, seilte han ut på havet og kom inn ved
1 CONT Hjaltland; men noen av skipene hans kom til Orknøyene. Kong Harald lå bare en kort tid før
1 CONT han seilte til Orknøyene, og derifra fikk han med seg en stor styrke og jarlene Pål og Erlend,
1 CONT sønnene til Torfinn jarl. Men han lot etter seg der dronning Ellisiv og døtrene deres, Maria og
1 CONT Ingegjerd. Derifra seilte han sør langs Skottland og så langs England og kom til land der det
1 CONT heter Klevland (i Yorkshire). Der gikk han i land og herjet straks og la under seg landet; han
1 CONT fikk ingen motstand. Siden styrte kong Harald inn til Skardaborg (Scarborough) og kjempet
1 CONT med bymennene der. Han gikk opp på berget som er der, og lot gjøre et stort bål, som han
1 CONT satte ild på. Da bålet flammet opp, tok de noen store staker og skubbet bålet ned i byen. Så
1 CONT tok det ene huset etter det andre til å brenne, og hele byen ga seg. Nå drepte nordmennene
1 CONT mange menn der, og tok alt det gods som de fikk tak i. Engelskmennene hadde da ikke annet
1 CONT vilkår enn å gi seg under kong Harald - om de ville berge livet. Da la han under seg alt land
1 CONT der han fór. Så styrte kong Harald med hele hæren sør langs landet og la til ved Hellornes
1 CONT (Holderness). Der kom det en flokk imot ham, og der holdt kong Harald slag og vant seier.
1 CONT 98. Olav, sønn til kong Harald, styrte bort fra England med hæren sin. De seilte ut fra Ravnsør
1 CONT (Ravenseer) og kom om høsten til Orknøyene. Der fikk de høre at Maria, datter til kong Harald
1 CONT Sigurdsson, hadde fått brådød samme dag og samme stund som hennes far kong Harald falt.
1 CONT Olav ble der om vinteren. Men sommeren etter fór kong Olav øst til Norge; der ble han så tatt
1 CONT til konge sammen med Magnus, sin bror. Dronning Ellisiv dro østover sammen med Olav, sin
1 CONT stesønn, og Ingegjerd hennes datter fulgte også med....?
0 @N6000000005599219211@ NOTE Elizabeth, and her two daughters sailed for England with Harald in 106 6.
