0 @N6000000001783604845@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Anna Yaroslavna was born between 1024 and 1032 - 1075, daughter of Yaroslav I of Kiev and his wife Ingegerd Olofsdotter, and was the queen consort of France as the wife of Henry I.  She became the regent for her son Philip I at He
1 CONC nri’s death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT After the death of his first wife, Matilda, King Henri searched the courts of Europe for a suitable bride, but could not locate a princess who was not related to him within illegal degrees of kinship. At last he sent an embassy to
1 CONC  distant Kiev, which returned with Anne (also called Agnes or Anna). Anne and Henri were married at the cathedral of Reims on May 19, 1051. They had three sons:
1 CONT
1 CONT Phillip II [Anne is credited with bringing the name Philip to Western Europe. She imported this Greek name (Philippos, from philos (love) and hippos (horse), meaning "the one that love horses") from her Eastern Orthodox culture].
1 CONT Hugh (1057 - October 18, 1102) - called the Great or Magnus, later Count of Crépi, who married the heiress of Vermandois and died on crusade in Tarsus, Cilicia.
1 CONT Robert (c. 1055-c. 1060)
1 CONT
1 CONT Regent
1 CONT
1 CONT For six years after Henry's death in 1060, she served as regent for Philip, who was only seven at the time. She was the first queen of France to serve as regent. Her co-regent was Count Baldwin V of Flanders. Anne was a literate w
1 CONC oman, rare for the time, but there was some opposition to her as regent on the grounds that her mastery of French was less than fluent.
1 CONT
1 CONT Second Marriage and Excommunication
1 CONT
1 CONT A year after the king's death, Anne, acting as regent, took a passionate fancy for Count Ralph III of Valois, a man whose political ambition encouraged him to repudiate his wife to marry Anne in 1062. Accused of adultery, Ralph's 
1 CONC wife appealed to Pope Alexander II, who excommunicated the couple. The young king Philip forgave his mother, which was just as well, since he was to find himself in a very similar predicament in the 1090s. Ralph died in September 
1 CONC 1074, at which time Anne returned to the French court.
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT She died in 1075, was buried at Villiers Abbey, La-Ferte-Alais, Essonne and her obits were celebrated on September 5.
1 CONT wikipedia
