0 @N6000000007329714918@ NOTE [Robert Leutner <rleutner -at- blue.weeg.uiowa.edu> Aug 27 '95]: Having
1 CONT re-connected with Anne of Kiev and found a couple of apparently good
1 CONT sources, I offer the following Ahnentafel of Anne for confirmation,
1 CONT correction, and comment. It is based primarily on the 1953 ed. of
1 CONT Isenburg's  Stammtafeln zur  Geschichte der Europaeischen Staaten  Tables
1 CONT 89 (Die GroBfuersten von  Kiew  912-1078, Fuersten von Halicz [Galizien]
1 CONT und Gorodno) and 77 (Die Koenige  von Schweden von Erich bis Erich XI.
1 CONT [900-1250]) with some additional  material from Samuel Hazzard Cross and
1 CONT Olgerd P. Sherowitz- Wetzor, ed.  and trans.,  The Russian Primary
1 CONT Chronicle: Laurentian Text (Cambridge,  Mass.: The Mediaeval Academy of
1 CONT America, 1953), pp 297-98 and chart  following.  (Since I have copies of
1 CONT these 2 Isenburg tables I'll be happy  to do lookups, assuming they
1 CONT haven't been superseded by later editions of  the  Stammtafeln .)  (Dates
1 CONT & other data in brackets are from Cross, et al.;  otherwise Isenburg.
1 CONT Comments by me in scrolled brackets.)
1 CONT 1    Anne of Kiev, d. after 1075.  Mar. 29 Jan 1044 [19 May 1051] Henry
1 CONT I,  King of France (b 1008, d 4 Aug 1060).
1 CONT 2    Yaroslav I, [Prince of Pereyaslavl' and Rostov-Suzdal' 988-1010,
1 CONT Pr.  of Novgorod 1010-1019], Great Prince of Kiev 1019, b 978, d  20 [19]
1 CONT Feb  1054, mar. (1) N. N., (2) 1019, Ingegard, da. of Olaf III, Sweden.
1 CONT 3    Ingegard (Anna), d 10 Feb 1050.
1 CONT 4    (St.) Vladimir, Pr. of Novgorod 973 [970-978], Gr. Pr. of Kiev 980
1 CONT [978-1015]; d 15 July 1015.  Isenburg gives marriages (1) Malfreda of
1 CONT Bohemia, d 1002, (2) 980 Rogneda, da. of Prince Rogwald von Polotzk,
1 CONT 'nun  from 989 on,' d 1002, (3) 989 Anna, dau. of Romanus II, Emperor of
1 CONT Byzantium, d 1011, and (4) Adelja [N. dau. of Cuno, Ct. of Oeningen, and
1 CONT granddau. of Otto I, Western Emperor, d 14 Aug 1018].  [Cross does not
1 CONT mention (1) and (2) above by name or date, but refers to '(before
1 CONT conversion) several wives.']
1 CONT 5    Malfreda of Bohemia, d 1002.
1 CONT 6    Olaf III, King of Sweden 995, d 1021/22, mar. Astrid (mother of
1 CONT Ingegard / Anna and Anund Jakob, King 1021/22); conc. Edla (mother of
1 CONT Edmund, K. 1051, d 1056, and Astrid, mar. Feb 1019, Olaf II, K of
1 CONT Norway).
1 CONT 7    Astrid.
1 CONT 8    Svyatoslav I, Gr. Pr. of Kiev 945-970 (independently from 956)
1 CONT [964-972], killed 973 [972], mar. Preslava of Hungary [no marriage
1 CONT given].
1 CONT 9    Predslava of Hungary.
1 CONT 12   Erik , K. of Sweden ca. 950, d. ca. 995, mar. Sigrid Storraade ,
1 CONT dau. of 'Skoglar Toste' .
1 CONT 13    Sigrid Storraade.
1 CONT 16   Igor I, b 875, Gr. Pr. of Kiev 912 [913], killed 945, mar. 903 [St.]
1 CONT Olga [aka Helen].
1 CONT 17   [St.] Olga [aka Helen], Regent 945-956, d 969.
1 CONT 24   Bjoern the Old, K. of Sweden 900, d. ca 950.
1 CONT 26   'Skoglar Toste' .
1 CONT 32   Rurik, Pr. of Novgorod 862, d 879.
1 CONT 48   Erik, K. of Sweden and 'Goten' , d  ca. 900.
1 CONT 96   Emund, 'Kg. zu Birka' .  //
