0 @N6000000002187757541@ NOTE Viacheslav I of Kiev
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Viacheslav Vladimirovich (???????? ???????????? in Russian) (1083-February 2, 1154), Prince of Smolensk (1113-1125), Turov (1125-1132, 1134-1146), Pereyaslavl (1132-1134, 1142), Peresopnitsa (1146-1149), Vyshgorod (1149-1151) and 
1 CONC Grand Prince of Kiev (1139, 1151-1154).
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a son of Vladimir Monomakh and Gytha of Wessex. On February 18, 1139 he succeeded his brother Yaropolk II of Kiev as Grand Prince, but was driven out in March by Vsevolod II of Kiev. He later ruled Kiev jointly with his nep
1 CONC hew Iziaslav II of Kiev and died not long after Iziaslav in late 1154 or early 1155 and is buried in the St. Sophia cathedral in Kiev. His only son, Michael Viacheslavovich, had predeceased him in 1129.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT Russian Primary Chronicle 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Mstislav of Kiev Grand Prince of Kiev Succeeded by
1 CONT Yuri Dolgoruki 
