1 CONT 'Colonial & Revolutionary Lineages in America', Vol 5, has Hugh's   wife
1 CONT was  ETIENETTE, dau of RAIMOND BERENGER II 'TOWHEAD', COUNT OF BARCELONA
1 CONT &  CARCASSONE (d. 1082) and MATILDA, dau of ROBERTO GISCARD. Could these
1 CONT two  Stephanies be one and the same, or is there disagrement between the
1 CONT sources on who Hugh's wife was ?
0 @N6000000001355771912@ NOTE Ramon Berenguer II, byname RAMON BERENGUER THE TOWHEAD, Catalan RAMONBERENGUER CAP D'ESTOPES (b. c. 1053--d. Dec. 5, 1082, between Barcelona and Gerona, Catalonia), count of Barcelona who reigned jointly withhis twin brother, Bere
1 CONC nguer Ramon II, from 1076 to 1082.
1 CONT Following up on the policies of their father, Ramon Berenguer I, theyproceeded to build the defenses and repopulate the lands that he had conquered. In 1082, in a forest en route to Gerona, Ramon Berenguer IIwas murdered, probably
1 CONC  by his brother, thereafter nicknamed "the Fratricide" ("el Fratricida"). Berenguer Ramon II, now sole master, took part in the civil wars of the Spanish Muslims and reconquered the Tarragona area (1091). He reigned until 1097, wh
1 CONC en, having lost a trial by combat that was intended to decide the question of his guilt in the crime attributed to him, he went on crusade to Jerusalem, where he died,probably in either 1097 or 1099.
