0 @N6000000002187757401@ NOTE Géza I of Hungary
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Géza I (Slovak: Gejza) (c. 1040 – 1077) was the king of the Kingdom of Hungary from 1074 to 1077.
1 CONT
1 CONT For his coronation, Géza received a crown from Byzantine Emperor Michael VII Dukas that was incorporated with the ancient crown of King Stephen I. Géza's short rule was characterized by general disorder in the kingdom. He did, how
1 CONC ever, capture Croatia from his brother-in-law Dmitar Zvonimir. He married twice; first to Sophia von Looz, daughter of the Count of Looz, and secondly to Synadene, a niece of Emperor Nicephorus III. By his first marriage, he had t
1 CONC wo children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Coloman of Hungary 
1 CONT Prince Álmos 
1 CONT Géza died on April 25, 1077 and was succeeded by his brother Ladislaus I. Géza is buried at Vác.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Solomon King of Hungary Succeeded by:
1 CONT Ladislaus I 
