1 CONC anding that Alexius meet with him: "Know, O King, that I am King ofKings, and superior to all, who are under the sky. You are nowpermitted to greet me, on my arrival, and to receive me withmagnificence, as befits my nobility." Ale
1 CONC xius was already wary of thearmies about to arrive, after the unruly mob led by Peter the Hermithad passed through earlier in the year. Alexius kept Hugh in custodyin a monastery until Hugh swore an oath of vassalage to him.
1 CONT
1 CONT After the Crusaders had successfully made their way across Seljukterritory and, in 1098, captured Antioch, Hugh was sent back toConstantinople to appeal for reinforcements from Alexius. Alexius wasuninterested, however, and Hugh, 
1 CONC instead of returning to Antioch tohelp plan the siege of Jerusalem, went back to France. There he wasscorned for not having fulfilled his vow as a Crusader to complete apilgrimage to Jerusalem, and Pope Paschal II threated to exco
