0 @N6000000000945065980@ NOTE Manuel var hærsjef i Bysants. 
1 CONT Han var meget ansett og av keiser Basilios II (976 - 1025) en meget begunstiget offiser
1 CONT fra det gamle Paflagonien i Lilleasien. Keiseren utnevnte ham til hærøverste i hele østlandet for
1 CONT å gjøre ende på det fiendlige forhold til Skleros.
0 @N6000000002187821184@ NOTE Manuel - This progenitor of the Comneni dynasty was a large landowner in Asia Minor whose home village was Comneni, which was near Hadrianople. His family grew in power and prestige, his first son and the son of his second son bot
1 CONC h becoming Emporers.  -http://www.aritek.com/hartgen/htm/comnenus_2.htm#name6163
1 CONT
1 CONT patrikios Manuel Erotikos Komnenos1,2
1 CONT b. 955, d. 1025, #5635
1 CONT Pedigree 
1 CONT       Strategos autokrator of the East. The Comneni came originally from Comne, near Hadrianople, and had estates in the Castamon district of Asia Minor. They were destined to play a preeminent role in Byzantium during the next hu
1 CONC ndred years.3 patrikios Manuel Erotikos Komnenos was born in 955 in the Castamon District, Paphlagonia, Pontica, Prefecture of Oriens, Byzantine Empire. He was the son of Isaakios Komnenos. Protospatharius, Prefect of the East in 
1 CONC Prefecture of Oriens, Byzantine Empire, between 976 and 1025.4 He served as Curopalates and Strategos under Basil II before 1025. He died in 1025 at age 70 years.  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Children of patrikios Manuel Erotikos Komnenos: 
1 CONT   basileus Rhomaiôn Isaakios I Komnenos+   b. c 1005, d. 1061 
1 CONT   domestikos ton scholon Ioannes I Komnenos+   b. 1015, d. 12 Jul 1067 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, Royalty for Commoners: The Complete Lineage of John of Gaunt, Son of Edward III, Kings of England, and Queen Philippa (.: ., 3rd Ed., 1998), 111-34. Hereinafter cited as RfC. 
1 CONT [S172] Various Encyclopaedea Britannica (U.S.A.: Encyclopaedea Britannica, Inc., 1976). Hereinafter cited as Encyclopaedea Britannica. 
1 CONT [S296] "Michael Psellus: Chronographia" The Chronographia composed by the most learned and right honourable monk Michael, in which are recounted the deeds of the following Emperors: Basil and Constantine, the Porphyrogeniti; their
1 CONC  successor, Romanus Argyropulus; Michael the Paphlagonian; Michael, nephew of the last-named, who originally had the title of Caesar; the two sisters Zoe and Theodora, also Porphyrogenitiae and both princesses; Constantine Monomac
1 CONC hus, who shared the throne with them; the princess Theodora, one of the aforementioned sisters, who ruled as Empress alone; Michael the Aged; Isaac Comnenus. The History ends with the proclamation of Constantine Ducas., Notes of B
1 CONC ook 7, Michael Psellus (A.D. 976-1077): Chronographia, online http://www.fordham.edu/halsall/basis/psellus-chrono-intro.html, printout dated January 1999. Previously published in hard copy (mailto:e-mail address?subject=Medieval S
1 CONC ourcebook Document: Medieval Sourcebook, 9 Oct 1952). Hereinafter cited as "Chronographia". 
1 CONT [S710] Charles P. Keith, The Ancestry of Benjamin Harrison, President of the United States of America 1889-1893, in Chart Form Showing Also the Descendants of William Henry Harrison, President of the United States of America in 18
1 CONC 41, and Notes on Families Related (Philadelphia, PA: J. B. Lippincott Company, 1893). Hereinafter cited as Harrison Ancestry. 
0 @N6000000004533643590@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Byzantine emperor Alexius I ComnenusThe Comnenus family was animportant family in the history of the Byzantine Empire.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Comneni originated in Paphlagonia, perhaps from the Kastamonucastle, which is possibly a corruption of Castra Comnenus. TheComnenus dynasty of Byzantine emperors was founded by Isaac IComnenus, a Stratopedarch of the East unde
1 CONC r Michael VI. In 1057 Isaacled a coup against Michael and was proclaimed emperor. However, thedynasty did not come to full power until the accession of Alexius IComnenus, Isaac I's nephew, in 1081.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Comneni were related to the Ducas and Angelus families. Alexius Imarried the grand-niece of Constantine X Ducas, a general who hadsucceeded Isaac in 1059. Their daughter Theodora married into theAngelus family; Theodora's gran
1 CONC dsons were the emperors Isaac IIAngelus and Alexius III Angelus.
1 CONT
1 CONT Under Alexius I and his successors the Empire was fairly prosperousand stable. Alexius moved the imperial palace to the Blachernaesection of Constantinople. Much of Anatolia was recovered from theSeljuk Turks, who had captured it 
1 CONC just prior to Alexius' reign.Alexius also saw the First Crusade pass through Byzantine territory,leading to the establishment of the Crusader states in the east. TheComnenus dynasty was very much involved in crusader affairs, and 
1 CONC alsointermarried with the royal families of the Principality of Antiochand the Kingdom of Jerusalem - Theodora, niece of Manuel I Comnenus,married Baldwin III of Jerusalem, and Maria, grand-niece of Manuel,married Amalric I of Jer
1 CONC usalem.
1 CONT
1 CONT Remarkably, despite the general tendency for Byzantine emperors to beoverthrown after a few years, Alexius ruled for 37, and his son JohnII ruled for 25, after uncovering a conspiracy against him by hissister, the chronicler Anna 
1 CONC Comnena, and her husband NicephorusBryennius. John's son Manuel ruled for another 37. Thereafter theComnenus dynasty fell into conspiracies and plots like many of theirancestors; Alexius II ruled for three years and his successorA
1 CONC ndronicus I ruled for two, overthrown by the Angelus family underIsaac I. The Angeli were overthrown during the Fourth Crusade in 1204,by a relative from the Ducas family.
1 CONT
1 CONT After the collapse of the empire in 1204, the Comneni fled back totheir homeland in Paphlagonia, and set up the Empire of Trebizond onthe Black Sea. The first emperor, also named Alexius I, was thegrandson of Andronicus I. These e
1 CONC mperors, the "Grand Comneni," as theywere known, ruled in Trebizond for over 250 years, until DavidComnenus was defeated by the Ottoman sultan Mehmed II.
1 CONT
1 CONT A renegade member of the Comnenus family, also named Isaac,established a separate "empire" on Cyprus in the 12th century. Theisland was taken from him by Richard I of England during the ThirdCrusade.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Byzantine Empire was restored in 1261 by the Palaeologus dynasty.
