0 @N6000000003949721610@ NOTE According to Ancestral Roots, Sigrid is not the daughter of the King of Poland. That was Gunnhild von Polen, who survived Erik and married Sven Forkbeard, following in Sigrid's footsteps, but Sigrid "divorced" (Viking style) Erik.
1 CONT Erik the Victorious was married several times. One of his wives is said to have been Sigrid Storrada ("great ruler'), the daughter of Skoglar Toste, a famous Viking from Vastergotland. According to Snorri, she was mother of Erik's
1 CONC  son Olof.
1 CONT About 985, according to the ancient tales, Erik fought a great battle against his still-rebellious nephew Stybjorn on the great plains of Fyrisvall, near Uppsala. . . . 
1 CONT Erik found it hard to get along with his wife Sigrid, due to her imperious temperament. After a while they went their separate ways. She retired to her estates in Vastergotland, where we are told that she ruled in great splendor a
1 CONC nd refused many suitors who were hungry for both her beauty and her lands. Among others, she is said to have refused Harald Granske of Norway and King Vifavald of Russia (a petty king of whom we know nothing further). Sigrid has b
1 CONC een called "the Haughty" and she seems to have truly earned this surname. [Royal Families of Medieval Scandinavia, Flanders, & Kiev]
1 CONT Note: From the above I assume that Sigrid "divorced" Erik a short while after the battle in 985.
0 @N6000000004533040701@ NOTE <b>Sigrid Storraade,</b> -o. 1000-, Dronning,
1 CONT var en Datter af den mægtige og rige Bonde og Viking Skaagul-Toste iGøtaland,
1 CONT efter hvem hun arvede mange Ejendomme. S. ægtede den svenske
1 CONT Konge Erik Sejersæl, med hvem hun havde Sønnen Olaf
1 CONT (Skotkonge) og Datteren Holmfrid, der blev gift med Hakon Jarls Søn
1 CONT Svend. Efter at være skilt fra Erik drog hun til sine Besiddelser
1 CONT i Gøtaland og havde her mange Bejlere, saaledes den norske
1 CONT Konge Harald Grænske og en russisk Konge Vsevolod, men hun
1 CONT lod begge indebrænde «for at gjøre Smaakonger lede af at fri til
1 CONT hende». Et Giftermaal med Olaf Tryggvason blev aftalt, men da
1 CONT han forlangte, at hun skulde antage Kristendommen, afslog hun at
1 CONT forlade sine Fædres Tro, hvorfor Olaf haanende slog hende i
1 CONT Ansigtet med sin Handske og kaldte hende en hedensk Hund. S.,
1 CONT der paa Grund af sine højtstræbende Planer havde faaet Navnet
1 CONT Storraade, ægtede derpaa Kong Svend Tveskjæg; hun havde med
1 CONT ham Datteren Estrid (IV, 603). S. ophidsede sin Ægtefælle mod
1 CONT den norske Konge, der desuden havde taget Svends Søster Thyre
1 CONT til Ægte uden hans Samtykke. I Forening med sin Stifsøn Kong
1 CONT Olaf overfaldt Svend Olaf Tryggvason ved Svold, og denne faldt
1 CONT (1000). Vi vide intet om S.s senere Skæbne eller hendes Dødsaar.
1 CONT I «Kong Valdemars Jordebog» nævnes endnu Sigridlef blandt den
1 CONT danske Konges Besiddelser i Sverige.
1 CONT
1 CONT <i>Johannes C. H. R. Steenstrup.</i>
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Sigrid the Haughty, Gunhilda, Sigrid Storråda, Swietoslawa, (967 -1014) was the daughter of mythical Burislav (almost certainly MieszkoI of Poland and Dubrawka). The medieval chroniclers generally confirmthe assumption that her fa
1 CONC ther was Mieszko I, but saga authors (mostimportant of which is Snorri Sturluson) put her father as SkogulToste.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 980 (possibly 985) she married Eric VI of Sweden. She may havegiven birth to Olof Skötkonung who later became king of Sweden, butsome doubt that.
1 CONT
1 CONT After 994 she married Sweyn I of Denmark under the name Gunhilda. Fromthis second marriage she probably had five children, including Canutethe Great and Harold II of Denmark.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her Slavic name is generally agreed as Swietoslawa, but only as areconstruction based on a single mention that her daughter was"Santslaue soror CNVTI regis nostri" from the "Liber vitae of the NewMinster and Hyde Abbey Winchester"
1 CONC  and assumption, that the earliermentioned daughter would be called after her mother.
0 @N6000000007329706398@ NOTE Oplysninger om hende fortaber sig i sagn og myter. Om hun overhovedet var
1 CONT gift med Svend er usikkert
0 @N6000000003635727100@ NOTE [1553] or "the Haughty"
0 @N6000000009304893964@ NOTE #Générale##Générale#l'adultère, 3ʻ femme et veuve d'Eric de Suède
