1 CONT Constance was the only daughter of Bohemund II of Antioch by his wifeAlice, princess of Jerusalem. She became princess of Antioch with onlyfour years old, under the regency of Baldwin II of Jerusalem(1130-1131) and Fulk of Jerusal
1 CONC em (1131-1136). In 1136, the control ofthe principality passed to Raymond of Poitiers, who became her husbandand co-ruler of Antioch in 1140. From this union three children wereborn:
1 CONT
1 CONT Bohemund III of Antioch, who succeeded her in 1163
1 CONT Mary of Antioch (1145-1182), married to Manuel I Comnenus
1 CONT Philippa of Antioch, married to Andronicus I Comnenus
1 CONT In 1149, Raymond died in the battle of Inab and Constance remarried in1153 with Raynald of Chatillon, who also became co-ruler of Antioch.Constance had two daughters from Raynald:
