0 @N6000000002187750290@ NOTE Dulce Berenguer
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Dulce Berenguer, Princess of Aragon, Queen Consort of Portugal (1152–1198) was first daughter of Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Barcelona and Petronila of Aragon. She was also the wife of Sancho I of Portugal.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1174 she was married to then Prince Sancho as part of an arrangement to secure an alliance between Aragon and Portugal by her brother Alfonso II of Aragon. With her husband's ascent to the throne in 1185, she became Queen Conso
1 CONC rt.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Children of Sancho and Dulce
1 CONT Name Birth Death Notes 
1 CONT Teresa of Portugal 1181 1250 Married to King Alfonso IX of Castile 
1 CONT Raymond c. 1180 1189   
1 CONT Sancha a. 1182 March 13, 1229 Abbess of Lorvão 
1 CONT Constance c. 1182 August 3, 1202   
1 CONT Afonso II April 23, 1185 March 25, 1223 Succeeded Sancho I of Portugal as 3rd King of Portugal 
1 CONT Peter February 23, 1187 June 2, 1258 Count of Urgell and Lord of the Balearic Islands, lived in León and married Arembiax Armengel, Countess of Urgell 
1 CONT Ferdinand March 24, 1188 March 4, 1233 Lived in France and married Jeanne of Flanders 
1 CONT Henry 1189 1189   
1 CONT Branca (Blanche) c. 1192 1240 Lady of Guadalajara 
1 CONT Berengária c. 1195 1221 Married to King Valdemar II of Denmark 
1 CONT Mafalda c. 1200 1256 Married to King Henry I of Castile 
