0 @N6000000002187821377@ NOTE Ivan Vladislav of Bulgaria
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ivan Vladislav was the ruler of Bulgaria from August or September 1015 to August or September 1018. He was the son of Aron, the brother of Samuil. His reign oversaw the annexation of Bulgaria by the Byzantine Empire.
1 CONT
1 CONT When Samuil ordered Aron and his family to be killed on suspicion of treason, Ivan ended up surviving only due to the insistance of his cousin Gavril Radomir. The Byzantines, who were having trouble dealing with Gavril Radomir upo
1 CONC n his rise to power, persuaded Ivan to kill the Bulgarian ruler, promising him the throne. He murdered Radomir near Ostrovo, and took his place as ruler of Bulgaria. However, despite swearing an oath of loyalty to Byzantine Empero
1 CONC r Basil II, the conflict with the Greeks continued. The Byzantines devastated Bulgaria, and finally took the capital Ohrid in 1018. Ivan himself was killed during the siege of Duras that same year.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ivan had a son, Alusian, that would play an influential role in Bulgaria's struggle for independence several decades later.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT History of Bulgaria 
1 CONT Comitopuli dynasty 
1 CONT Bitola inscription 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Gavril Radomir List of Bulgarian monarchs Succeeded by:
1 CONT None 
0 @N6000000003949911110@ NOTE He murdered his cousin Tsar Gavriil Radomir, succeeding him in 1015 as IVAN VLADISLAV Tsar of the Bulgarians.  He reconquered Duklja in 1016 after murdering Knez Ivan Vladimir[66].  He was killed by the Byzantines during an unsucc
1 CONC essful attempt to recapture Durazzo, after which Emperor Basileios II made his solemn entry to Ochrida where he received homage from the remaining members of the family of the Tsar and annexed Bulgaria, which was divided into thre
1 CONC e themes
0 @N6000000000437110897@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Bulgaria
0 @N6000000002187821389@ NOTE Marija of Byzantium1
1 CONT b. 972, d. 1029, #5629 
1 CONT      Marija of Byzantium was born in 972. She married Ivan Vladislav, Tsar of Bulgaria, son of Aaron Amitopulos Kometopoulos.1,2,3 She was a "girdled Patrician" circa 990 in Constantinople, Byzanitum.1 She died in 1029 at age 57 y
1 CONC ears.3  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Children of Marija of Byzantium and Ivan Vladislav, Tsar of Bulgaria: 
1 CONT   Presian II, Tsar of Bulgaria   b. c 992?, d. bt 1061 - 1061 
1 CONT   Trajan Kometopoulos+   b. c 995, d. 1018 
1 CONT   Ekaterina Kometopoulos+   b. c 1015 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, Royalty for Commoners: The Complete Lineage of John of Gaunt, Son of Edward III, Kings of England, and Queen Philippa (.: ., 3rd Ed., 1998), 309-35. Hereinafter cited as RfC. 
1 CONT [S464] "Medieval Royal Families of the Balkans" This will be a series of pieces attempting to account for the genealogy of the medieval rulers of the Balkans. There are lots of uncertainties about these lines, since many records h
1 CONC ave not survived. Source materials for most things in the medieval Balkans are ususally not from contemporary writers, and the few contemporary sources existing are usually from Byzantine writers, not writers from the various stat
1 CONC es themselves. The tables I'm about to present are based on Europaeische Stammtafeln, but modified by some recent scholarship by John V. A. Fine in his two books, "The Early Medieval Balkans" and "The Late Medieval Balkans". - PT
1 CONT , Paul Theroff's Royal Genealogy Site - Royal Families of the Balkans, online Medieval Royal Families of the Balkans, printout dated 5/9/00. Previously published in hard copy (e-mail address: Paul Theroff, 4/24/99). Hereinafter ci
1 CONC ted as "Theroff-Balkans". 
1 CONT [S1578] Ian S. R. Mladjov, "Reconsidering Agatha, Wife of Eadward the Exile", The Plantagenet Connection Summer/Winter (2003). Hereinafter cited as "Reconsidering Agatha". 
0 @N6000000000437562250@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Bulgaria
0 @N6000000002187823039@ NOTE Romanos Aballantes1
1 CONT b. circa 978, #12776 
1 CONT      Romanos Aballantes was born circa 978. He married N. N. Kourkouaina, daughter of Theodoras Kourkouas and N. N. Phocaina, before 1000.1  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Child of Romanos Aballantes and N. N. Kourkouaina: 
1 CONT   Kontostephane Aballanta+   b. c 1000 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, Royalty for Commoners: The Complete Lineage of John of Gaunt, Son of Edward III, Kings of England, and Queen Philippa (.: ., 3rd Ed., 1998), 370-35. Hereinafter cited as RfC.
0 @N6000000002187823251@ NOTE Adrian Dalassenos1
1 CONT b. circa 975, #9109
1 CONT Pedigree 
1 CONT      Adrian Dalassenos was born circa 975. He was the son of Theophylactos Dalassenos. He was was exiled between 1038 and 1039.  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Child of Adrian Dalassenos: 
1 CONT   N. N. Dalassena+   b. c 995 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, Royalty for Commoners: The Complete Lineage of John of Gaunt, Son of Edward III, Kings of England, and Queen Philippa (.: ., 3rd Ed., 1998), 96-34. Hereinafter cited as RfC. 
