1 CONT Svend I (known in England as Sweyn) Forkbeard was King of England in the autumn of 1013 and King of Denmark about 985. He had two sons: Harald II Svendsen, King of Denmark on 3 February 1014; and Knud (Cnut or Canute) I, "The Grea
1 CONC t", King of England and Denmark in 1019, also King of Norway 1028, Lord of Norse Colonies, Overlord of the Scots, King of Dublin (?).
